window.REV_FLIP=window.REV_FLIP||{};window.REV_FLIP["az-900"]=[{"id":"az-900-f0001","card":"q-az-900-001-overview","sec":"az-900-s001","q":"Does the AZ-900 exam test CLI command syntax, and why do the study notes still show commands?","a":"<p>No. AZ-900 does not test command syntax. The CLI, PowerShell and SDK demos are illustrative: they show what each service does.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0002","card":"q-az-900-001-overview","sec":"az-900-s001","q":"In AZ-900 code demos, what must you do with placeholders like <code>&lt;sub-id&gt;</code>?","a":"<p>Replace them with your own real values before running the command.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0003","card":"q-az-900-001-overview","sec":"az-900-s001","q":"Which areas does the AZ-900 study outline cover, in order?","a":"<ol>\n  <li>Exam scope and terminology updates</li>\n  <li>Cloud concepts: models and shared responsibility</li>\n  <li>Benefits of cloud: availability, scale, reliability, governance</li>\n  <li>Service types: IaaS, PaaS, SaaS</li>\n  <li>Core architecture: regions, zones, resources</li>\n  <li>Compute and networking</li>\n  <li>Storage and data migration</li>\n  <li>Identity, access and security</li>\n  <li>Cost management</li>\n  <li>Governance and compliance</li>\n  <li>Managing and deploying resources</li>\n  <li>Monitoring tools</li>\n  <li>Scenario walkthroughs</li>\n</ol>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0004","card":"q-az-900-002-1-exam-scope-and-terminology-updates","sec":"az-900-s002","q":"What are the four AZ-900 exam domains?","a":"<p>Cloud concepts, Architecture and services, Identity, access, security, and Management and governance.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0005","card":"q-az-900-002-1-exam-scope-and-terminology-updates","sec":"az-900-s002","q":"Which topics belong to the AZ-900 \"Cloud concepts\" domain?","a":"<p>Cloud computing, public/private/hybrid, high availability, scalability, agility, security, governance, manageability, IaaS/PaaS/SaaS and serverless.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0006","card":"q-az-900-002-1-exam-scope-and-terminology-updates","sec":"az-900-s002","q":"Which topics belong to the AZ-900 \"Architecture and services\" domain?","a":"<p>Regions, data centers, resource management, compute, networking, VMs, VNets, storage and redundancy.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0007","card":"q-az-900-002-1-exam-scope-and-terminology-updates","sec":"az-900-s002","q":"Which topics belong to the AZ-900 \"Identity, access, security\" domain?","a":"<p>Security concepts, Entra ID (Azure AD), RBAC and Defender for Cloud.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0008","card":"q-az-900-002-1-exam-scope-and-terminology-updates","sec":"az-900-s002","q":"Which topics belong to the AZ-900 \"Management and governance\" domain?","a":"<p>Costs, CLI tools, Arc, ARM/IaC and Azure Monitor.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0009","card":"q-az-900-002-1-exam-scope-and-terminology-updates","sec":"az-900-s002","q":"What is Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) called now, and what is Azure AD Domain Services called?","a":"<p>Azure AD is now <strong>Microsoft Entra ID</strong>. Azure AD Domain Services is now <strong>Microsoft Entra Domain Services</strong>. <em>Microsoft Entra</em> is the product family, and Entra ID is one product in it. The commands are unchanged.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0010","card":"q-az-900-002-1-exam-scope-and-terminology-updates","sec":"az-900-s002","q":"What was added to the AZ-900 cloud-concepts domain in July 2023, and what does it mean?","a":"<p><strong>Serverless</strong>. The provider provisions, scales and manages the infrastructure, and you only write code.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0011","card":"q-az-900-002-1-exam-scope-and-terminology-updates","sec":"az-900-s002","q":"What was added to the AZ-900 managing-and-deploying domain in July 2023?","a":"<p><strong>Infrastructure as Code (IaC)</strong>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0012","card":"q-az-900-002-1-exam-scope-and-terminology-updates","sec":"az-900-s002","q":"What other AZ-900 updates were wording only?","a":"<p>Capitalization, \"MFA\" spelled out, \"defense-in-depth\" hyphenated, and \"external identities, including B2B and B2C\".</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0013","card":"q-az-900-002-1-exam-scope-and-terminology-updates","sec":"az-900-s002","q":"Which Azure CLI commands install the CLI on macOS, sign in, and list your subscriptions as a table?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>brew install azure-cli\naz login\naz account list --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0014","card":"q-az-900-002-1-exam-scope-and-terminology-updates","sec":"az-900-s002","q":"Which Azure CLI command sets the active subscription, and which lists the available regions?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az account set --subscription &quot;&lt;subscription-name-or-id&gt;&quot;\naz account list-locations --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0015","card":"q-az-900-002-1-exam-scope-and-terminology-updates","sec":"az-900-s002","q":"Which Azure PowerShell commands install the Az module, sign in, list subscriptions and set the active subscription?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">PowerShell</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Install-Module -Name Az -AllowClobber -Scope CurrentUser\nConnect-AzAccount\nGet-AzSubscription | Format-Table\nSet-AzContext -SubscriptionName &quot;&lt;subscription-name&gt;&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0016","card":"q-az-900-002-1-exam-scope-and-terminology-updates","sec":"az-900-s002","q":"Which Azure CLI commands list Entra ID users and groups as a table?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az ad user list --output table\naz ad group list --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0017","card":"q-az-900-002-1-exam-scope-and-terminology-updates","sec":"az-900-s002","q":"Which Azure CLI command creates an Entra ID user?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az ad user create \\\n  --display-name &quot;John Doe&quot; \\\n  --user-principal-name john@contoso.onmicrosoft.com \\\n  --password &quot;&lt;password&gt;&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0018","card":"q-az-900-003-2-cloud-concepts-models-and-shared-respo","sec":"az-900-s003","q":"What ideas does cloud computing bundle together?","a":"<p>Shared responsibility, service models, scalability, availability, and pay-for-what-you-use.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0019","card":"q-az-900-004-shared-responsibility-model","sec":"az-900-s004","q":"In Azure, what is the shared responsibility model?","a":"<p>You and the cloud provider share responsibility. The provider never takes all of it.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0020","card":"q-az-900-004-shared-responsibility-model","sec":"az-900-s004","q":"Why is a bug in your own app still your problem in the cloud?","a":"<p>The provider only covers what it controls.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0021","card":"q-az-900-004-shared-responsibility-model","sec":"az-900-s004","q":"How does the service type (IaaS, PaaS, SaaS) change who is responsible?","a":"<p>The service type decides how much falls on you. Moving IaaS to PaaS to SaaS shifts responsibility to the provider.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0022","card":"q-az-900-005-cloud-models","sec":"az-900-s005","q":"What is a public cloud?","a":"<p>Shared provider infrastructure that is <strong>multi-tenant</strong>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0023","card":"q-az-900-005-cloud-models","sec":"az-900-s005","q":"What is a private cloud?","a":"<p>Infrastructure dedicated to one company. It is <strong>single-tenant</strong>, and it is self-owned or third-party hosted.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0024","card":"q-az-900-005-cloud-models","sec":"az-900-s005","q":"What is a hybrid cloud?","a":"<p>A mix of public and private cloud.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0025","card":"q-az-900-005-cloud-models","sec":"az-900-s005","q":"What are the pros of the public cloud?","a":"<p>Agility, quick deployment, easy management, pay-as-you-go, and cost-tracking tools.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0026","card":"q-az-900-005-cloud-models","sec":"az-900-s005","q":"What are the cons of the public cloud?","a":"<p>Less control and flexibility, regulatory limits, and data on shared systems.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0027","card":"q-az-900-005-cloud-models","sec":"az-900-s005","q":"What are the pros of the private cloud?","a":"<p>The same agility, a private network, and it can run without internet (it syncs later, for example on cruise ships). There are also no cloud provider fees.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0028","card":"q-az-900-005-cloud-models","sec":"az-900-s005","q":"What are the cons of the private cloud?","a":"<p>High upfront cost (hardware, staff, power), a third-party provider that owns the systems holding your data, and management overhead.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0029","card":"q-az-900-005-cloud-models","sec":"az-900-s005","q":"What are the pros of the hybrid cloud?","a":"<p>You keep sensitive systems (for example a database) on-prem, you support legacy systems, and you get more control over data.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0030","card":"q-az-900-005-cloud-models","sec":"az-900-s005","q":"What are the cons of the hybrid cloud?","a":"<p>Complex setup and troubleshooting, data compatibility with older databases, and a need for IT expertise.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0031","card":"q-az-900-006-cloud-models","sec":"az-900-s005","q":"How do you choose between public, private and hybrid cloud?","a":"<p>List your requirements (management, privacy, security, cost), weigh each model against them, then pick.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0032","card":"q-az-900-006-cloud-models","sec":"az-900-s005","q":"Which cloud model fits \"low cost\"?","a":"<p>Public, because it is pay-as-you-go. Private is not a fit (high upfront cost). Hybrid is mixed.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0033","card":"q-az-900-006-cloud-models","sec":"az-900-s005","q":"Which cloud models give full control?","a":"<p>Private gives full control. Public does not. Hybrid gives partial control.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0034","card":"q-az-900-006-cloud-models","sec":"az-900-s005","q":"Which cloud models work with no internet needed?","a":"<p>Private works without internet. Public does not. Hybrid is partial.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0035","card":"q-az-900-006-cloud-models","sec":"az-900-s005","q":"Which cloud model is best for quick deployment?","a":"<p>Public. Private is slower, and hybrid is complex.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0036","card":"q-az-900-006-cloud-models","sec":"az-900-s005","q":"Which cloud models suit strict security or regulatory needs, and which suit legacy support?","a":"<p>Private and hybrid both fit strict security/regulatory needs (public is challenging). Private and hybrid also support legacy systems. Public does not.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0037","card":"q-az-900-006-cloud-models","sec":"az-900-s005","q":"Which Azure CLI commands create a resource group and a VM in public cloud, as an example of agility?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az group create --name myPublicRG --location eastus\n\naz vm create \\\n  --resource-group myPublicRG \\\n  --name myPublicVM \\\n  --image Ubuntu2204 \\\n  --size Standard_B2s \\\n  --admin-username azureuser \\\n  --generate-ssh-keys</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0038","card":"q-az-900-006-cloud-models","sec":"az-900-s005","q":"Which Azure CLI commands resize a VM up and back down, and delete the whole resource group to stop paying?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az vm resize --resource-group myPublicRG --name myPublicVM --size Standard_D4s_v3\n\naz vm resize --resource-group myPublicRG --name myPublicVM --size Standard_B2s\n\naz group delete --name myPublicRG --yes --no-wait</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0039","card":"q-az-900-006-cloud-models","sec":"az-900-s005","q":"In a hybrid cloud with a VPN, which Azure CLI command creates the virtual network and its gateway subnet?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az network vnet create \\\n  --resource-group myHybridRG \\\n  --name myAzureVNet \\\n  --address-prefix 10.0.0.0/16 \\\n  --subnet-name GatewaySubnet \\\n  --subnet-prefix 10.0.1.0/24</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0040","card":"q-az-900-006-cloud-models","sec":"az-900-s005","q":"In a hybrid cloud, which Azure CLI command creates the VPN gateway that connects Azure to on-prem?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az network vnet-gateway create \\\n  --resource-group myHybridRG \\\n  --name myVPNGateway \\\n  --vnet myAzureVNet \\\n  --gateway-type Vpn \\\n  --vpn-type RouteBased \\\n  --sku VpnGw1</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0041","card":"q-az-900-006-cloud-models","sec":"az-900-s005","q":"In a hybrid cloud, which Azure CLI command creates the local network gateway that represents the on-prem network?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az network local-gateway create \\\n  --resource-group myHybridRG \\\n  --name myOnPremGateway \\\n  --gateway-ip-address &lt;your-on-prem-public-ip&gt; \\\n  --local-address-prefixes 192.168.0.0/24</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0042","card":"q-az-900-007-consumption-based-model","sec":"az-900-s006","q":"In Azure's consumption-based model, what do you pay for?","a":"<p>What is <strong>allocated</strong> to you, not what you actively use. A running idle VM is still billed.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0043","card":"q-az-900-007-consumption-based-model","sec":"az-900-s006","q":"What are the two cost-control rules in the Azure consumption-based model?","a":"<ol>\n  <li>Do not allocate more than you need (do not provision 8 cores when 2 will do).</li>\n  <li>Fully use what you allocate (do not leave resources idle).</li>\n</ol>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0044","card":"q-az-900-007-consumption-based-model","sec":"az-900-s006","q":"What Azure features help with both cost-control rules?","a":"<p>Auto-scaling, cost alerts and recommendations.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0045","card":"q-az-900-007-consumption-based-model","sec":"az-900-s006","q":"Which Azure CLI commands create a right-sized VM (2 cores, 4 GB RAM) instead of an oversized one?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az vm create --resource-group myRG --name myVM --size Standard_B2s --image Ubuntu2204</code></pre></div>\n<p>The oversized version (8 cores, 32 GB RAM) uses <code>--size Standard_D8s_v3</code> for a workload that needs only 2 cores.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0046","card":"q-az-900-007-consumption-based-model","sec":"az-900-s006","q":"Which Azure CLI commands stop compute charges for a VM and start it again?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az vm deallocate --name myVM --resource-group myRG\n\naz vm start --name myVM --resource-group myRG</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0047","card":"q-az-900-007-consumption-based-model","sec":"az-900-s006","q":"Which Python SDK loop lists all VMs and their sizes to audit allocation?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>for vm in compute_client.virtual_machines.list_all():\n    print(f&quot;VM: {vm.name}, Size: {vm.hardware_profile.vm_size}, Location: {vm.location}&quot;)</code></pre></div>\n<p>It uses <code>ComputeManagementClient(credential, \"&lt;subscription-id&gt;\")</code> with <code>DefaultAzureCredential()</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0048","card":"q-az-900-008-high-availability","sec":"az-900-s007","q":"What is availability, and what is high availability?","a":"<p><strong>Availability</strong> means the app and its systems are accessible to users. <strong>High availability</strong> is 99% or higher, achieved with redundant systems.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0049","card":"q-az-900-008-high-availability","sec":"az-900-s007","q":"What threats reduce availability?","a":"<p>Network outage, application failure, system (VM) outage, power outage, and failure of a system you depend on (such as a database server).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0050","card":"q-az-900-008-high-availability","sec":"az-900-s007","q":"What downtime per year and per month does a 99% SLA allow?","a":"<p>3.65 days per year and 7.3 hours per month.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0051","card":"q-az-900-008-high-availability","sec":"az-900-s007","q":"What downtime per year and per month does a 99.9% SLA allow?","a":"<p>8.76 hours per year and 43.8 minutes per month.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0052","card":"q-az-900-008-high-availability","sec":"az-900-s007","q":"What downtime per year and per month does a 99.95% SLA allow?","a":"<p>4.38 hours per year and 21.9 minutes per month.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0053","card":"q-az-900-008-high-availability","sec":"az-900-s007","q":"What downtime per year and per month does a 99.99% SLA allow?","a":"<p>52.6 minutes per year and 4.38 minutes per month.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0054","card":"q-az-900-008-high-availability","sec":"az-900-s007","q":"Which Azure CLI command deploys a VM into Availability Zone 1 for high availability?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az vm create \\\n  --resource-group myRG \\\n  --name myHA-VM \\\n  --image Ubuntu2204 \\\n  --size Standard_B2s \\\n  --zone 1 \\\n  --admin-username azureuser \\\n  --generate-ssh-keys</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0055","card":"q-az-900-008-high-availability","sec":"az-900-s007","q":"Which Azure CLI command creates an availability set, and what does an availability set protect against?","a":"<p>It protects against hardware failures within a datacenter.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az vm availability-set create \\\n  --resource-group myRG \\\n  --name myAvailabilitySet \\\n  --platform-fault-domain-count 2 \\\n  --platform-update-domain-count 5</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0056","card":"q-az-900-008-high-availability","sec":"az-900-s007","q":"Which Azure CLI command checks the availability status of a VM?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az vm get-instance-view \\\n  --resource-group myRG \\\n  --name myVM \\\n  --query &quot;instanceView.statuses[1]&quot; \\\n  --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0057","card":"q-az-900-008-high-availability","sec":"az-900-s007","q":"Which Python SDK code reads the status of a VM across a subscription?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>for vm in compute.virtual_machines.list_all():\n    instance_view = compute.virtual_machines.instance_view(\n        vm.id.split(&quot;/&quot;)[4],  # resource group\n        vm.name\n    )\n    status = instance_view.statuses[-1].display_status\n    print(f&quot;{vm.name}: {status}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0058","card":"q-az-900-009-scalability","sec":"az-900-s008","q":"In Azure, what are scale up, scale down, scale out and scale in?","a":"<p><strong>Scale up</strong> (vertical): move to a more powerful machine. <strong>Scale down</strong> (vertical): move to a less powerful machine. <strong>Scale out</strong> (horizontal): add more identical instances, which needs a <strong>load balancer</strong>. <strong>Scale in</strong> (horizontal): remove instances.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0059","card":"q-az-900-009-scalability","sec":"az-900-s008","q":"What is the difference between agility and elasticity in the cloud?","a":"<p><strong>Agility</strong> is how easy it is to add or remove resources. <strong>Elasticity</strong> is scaling automatically with demand, in both directions (the rubber-band analogy).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0060","card":"q-az-900-009-scalability","sec":"az-900-s008","q":"Which Azure CLI commands scale a VM up, scale it down, and list available VM sizes in a region?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az vm resize \\\n  --resource-group myRG \\\n  --name myVM \\\n  --size Standard_D4s_v3\n\naz vm resize \\\n  --resource-group myRG \\\n  --name myVM \\\n  --size Standard_B2s\n\naz vm list-sizes --location eastus --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0061","card":"q-az-900-009-scalability","sec":"az-900-s008","q":"Which Python SDK lines scale up a VM to <code>Standard_D4s_v3</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>vm = compute.virtual_machines.get(&quot;myRG&quot;, &quot;myVM&quot;)\n\nvm.hardware_profile.vm_size = &quot;Standard_D4s_v3&quot;\ncompute.virtual_machines.begin_create_or_update(&quot;myRG&quot;, &quot;myVM&quot;, vm)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0062","card":"q-az-900-010-scalability","sec":"az-900-s008","q":"Which Azure CLI command creates a Virtual Machine Scale Set (VMSS) with 2 instances behind a load balancer?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az vmss create \\\n  --resource-group myRG \\\n  --name myScaleSet \\\n  --image Ubuntu2204 \\\n  --vm-sku Standard_B2s \\\n  --instance-count 2 \\\n  --admin-username azureuser \\\n  --generate-ssh-keys \\\n  --load-balancer myLoadBalancer</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0063","card":"q-az-900-010-scalability","sec":"az-900-s008","q":"Which Azure CLI commands scale a VMSS out to 4 instances and back in to 2?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az vmss scale \\\n  --resource-group myRG \\\n  --name myScaleSet \\\n  --new-capacity 4\n\naz vmss scale \\\n  --resource-group myRG \\\n  --name myScaleSet \\\n  --new-capacity 2</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0064","card":"q-az-900-010-scalability","sec":"az-900-s008","q":"Which Azure CLI command enables autoscaling on a VMSS with a minimum of 2 and a maximum of 10 instances?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az monitor autoscale create \\\n  --resource-group myRG \\\n  --resource myScaleSet \\\n  --resource-type Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachineScaleSets \\\n  --name myAutoscale \\\n  --min-count 2 \\\n  --max-count 10 \\\n  --count 2</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0065","card":"q-az-900-010-scalability","sec":"az-900-s008","q":"Which Azure CLI command adds an autoscale rule that scales out by 2 when average CPU is over 70% for 5 minutes?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az monitor autoscale rule create \\\n  --resource-group myRG \\\n  --autoscale-name myAutoscale \\\n  --condition &quot;Percentage CPU &gt; 70 avg 5m&quot; \\\n  --scale out 2</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0066","card":"q-az-900-010-scalability","sec":"az-900-s008","q":"Which Azure CLI command adds an autoscale rule that scales in by 1 when average CPU is under 30% for 5 minutes?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az monitor autoscale rule create \\\n  --resource-group myRG \\\n  --autoscale-name myAutoscale \\\n  --condition &quot;Percentage CPU &lt; 30 avg 5m&quot; \\\n  --scale in 1</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0067","card":"q-az-900-011-reliability-and-predictability","sec":"az-900-s009","q":"What is a fault, and what is fault tolerance?","a":"<p>A <strong>fault</strong> is a failure (network, power, hardware). <strong>Fault tolerance</strong> means you survive a fault and stay available.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0068","card":"q-az-900-011-reliability-and-predictability","sec":"az-900-s009","q":"Which Azure mechanisms give fault tolerance?","a":"<p>Availability zones and geo-redundant storage.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0069","card":"q-az-900-011-reliability-and-predictability","sec":"az-900-s009","q":"What is a disaster in cloud terms, and what do you plan with?","a":"<p>A <strong>disaster</strong> is a large-scale event (hurricane, flood, fire). You plan with <strong>BCDR</strong> (Business Continuity and Disaster Recovery).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0070","card":"q-az-900-011-reliability-and-predictability","sec":"az-900-s009","q":"What do Azure Site Recovery and Azure Backup do?","a":"<p>Azure Site Recovery replicates VMs to another region. Azure Backup protects VMs with automated backups.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0071","card":"q-az-900-011-reliability-and-predictability","sec":"az-900-s009","q":"Which Azure CLI commands create a backup vault and enable backup for a VM with the default policy?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az backup vault create \\\n  --resource-group myRG \\\n  --name myBackupVault \\\n  --location eastus\n\naz backup protection enable-for-vm \\\n  --resource-group myRG \\\n  --vault-name myBackupVault \\\n  --vm myVM \\\n  --policy-name DefaultPolicy</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0072","card":"q-az-900-012-security-and-governance","sec":"az-900-s010","q":"What is the difference between security and governance in the cloud?","a":"<p><strong>Security</strong> restricts access to authorized people only. <strong>Governance</strong> covers what access someone has, what they can do, and how. It is driven by regulations, company policy and cost control.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0073","card":"q-az-900-012-security-and-governance","sec":"az-900-s010","q":"What does the cloud provider supply for security and governance?","a":"<p>Documentation and services that find and fix security or governance gaps, often before they affect you.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0074","card":"q-az-900-012-security-and-governance","sec":"az-900-s010","q":"Which Azure CLI command creates a Network Security Group (NSG)?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az network nsg create \\\n  --resource-group myRG \\\n  --name myNSG</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0075","card":"q-az-900-012-security-and-governance","sec":"az-900-s010","q":"Which Azure CLI command allows only SSH (port 22) from a specific IP range in an NSG?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az network nsg rule create \\\n  --resource-group myRG \\\n  --nsg-name myNSG \\\n  --name AllowSSH \\\n  --priority 100 \\\n  --source-address-prefixes &quot;203.0.113.0/24&quot; \\\n  --destination-port-ranges 22 \\\n  --access Allow \\\n  --protocol Tcp</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0076","card":"q-az-900-012-security-and-governance","sec":"az-900-s010","q":"Which Azure CLI command denies all other inbound traffic in an NSG?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az network nsg rule create \\\n  --resource-group myRG \\\n  --nsg-name myNSG \\\n  --name DenyAllInbound \\\n  --priority 200 \\\n  --source-address-prefixes &quot;*&quot; \\\n  --destination-port-ranges &quot;*&quot; \\\n  --access Deny \\\n  --protocol &quot;*&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0077","card":"q-az-900-013-manageability","sec":"az-900-s011","q":"What does manageability mean in the cloud, and what does the cloud provide for it?","a":"<p>The cloud is not \"click and forget\". It provides monitoring, manual and automatic scaling, budgets with proactive alerts, and many deployment routes (templates, CLI, SDKs, portal).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0078","card":"q-az-900-013-manageability","sec":"az-900-s011","q":"Which Azure CLI command creates an alert when VM CPU exceeds 80%?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az monitor metrics alert create \\\n  --name HighCPUAlert \\\n  --resource-group myRG \\\n  --scopes &quot;/subscriptions/&lt;sub-id&gt;/resourceGroups/myRG/providers/Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/myVM&quot; \\\n  --condition &quot;avg Percentage CPU &gt; 80&quot; \\\n  --window-size 5m \\\n  --evaluation-frequency 1m \\\n  --description &quot;Alert when CPU exceeds 80%&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0079","card":"q-az-900-013-manageability","sec":"az-900-s011","q":"Which Azure CLI command sets a monthly budget of 200?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az consumption budget create \\\n  --budget-name MonthlyLimit \\\n  --amount 200 \\\n  --time-grain Monthly \\\n  --start-date 2024-01-01 \\\n  --end-date 2024-12-31 \\\n  --resource-group myRG</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0080","card":"q-az-900-013-manageability","sec":"az-900-s011","q":"Which Azure CLI command views the month-to-date actual cost?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az cost management query \\\n  --type ActualCost \\\n  --timeframe MonthToDate \\\n  --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0081","card":"q-az-900-013-manageability","sec":"az-900-s011","q":"Which Azure CLI commands show different management interfaces: interactive mode, one-command web app deploy, and a Bicep Infrastructure as Code deployment?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az interactive          # Interactive CLI mode\naz webapp up            # Deploy a web app in one command\naz deployment group create --template-file main.bicep  # Infrastructure as Code</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0082","card":"q-az-900-013-manageability","sec":"az-900-s011","q":"Which PowerShell command reads the CPU metric of a VM?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">PowerShell</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Get-AzMetric -ResourceId &quot;/subscriptions/&lt;sub-id&gt;/resourceGroups/myRG/providers/Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/myVM&quot; `\n  -MetricName &quot;Percentage CPU&quot; `\n  -TimeGrain 00:05:00 `\n  -StartTime (Get-Date).AddHours(-1)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0083","card":"q-az-900-014-4-service-types-iaas-paas-saas","sec":"az-900-s012","q":"In IaaS, PaaS and SaaS, what does the provider manage?","a":"<p>IaaS: hardware, networking and storage. PaaS: those plus OS, middleware and runtime. SaaS: everything.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0084","card":"q-az-900-014-4-service-types-iaas-paas-saas","sec":"az-900-s012","q":"In IaaS, PaaS and SaaS, what do you manage?","a":"<p>IaaS: OS, middleware, runtime, apps and data. PaaS: apps and data. SaaS: data and configuration (sometimes nothing).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0085","card":"q-az-900-014-4-service-types-iaas-paas-saas","sec":"az-900-s012","q":"How do IaaS, PaaS and SaaS compare on control, management burden and ease of use?","a":"<p>Control and flexibility: IaaS most, PaaS moderate (the provider makes many choices), SaaS least. Responsibility and management burden: IaaS highest, PaaS moderate, SaaS lowest. Ease of use: IaaS least, PaaS moderate, SaaS most.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0086","card":"q-az-900-014-4-service-types-iaas-paas-saas","sec":"az-900-s012","q":"How is each of IaaS, PaaS and SaaS billed?","a":"<p>IaaS and PaaS are billed by consumption. SaaS is pay-as-you-go or free.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0087","card":"q-az-900-014-4-service-types-iaas-paas-saas","sec":"az-900-s012","q":"What is the Azure example for IaaS, PaaS and SaaS?","a":"<p>IaaS: Virtual Machines. PaaS: App Service. SaaS: Microsoft 365. Other SaaS examples are Outlook.com, OneDrive, Salesforce and Gmail.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0088","card":"q-az-900-014-4-service-types-iaas-paas-saas","sec":"az-900-s012","q":"When do you use IaaS, PaaS or SaaS?","a":"<p>IaaS when you need full control of OS and runtime. PaaS when you want to focus on the app, not infrastructure (it has turnkey features: turn on, configure, done). SaaS when you just need to use software (web, phone or desktop app).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0089","card":"q-az-900-014-4-service-types-iaas-paas-saas","sec":"az-900-s012","q":"With an IaaS VM, what are you responsible for?","a":"<p>Patching the OS, installing software, opening ports, monitoring, scaling and backing up.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0090","card":"q-az-900-014-4-service-types-iaas-paas-saas","sec":"az-900-s012","q":"Which Azure CLI commands create a resource group and an IaaS VM?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az group create --name myIaaSRG --location eastus\n\naz vm create \\\n  --resource-group myIaaSRG \\\n  --name myIaaSVM \\\n  --image Ubuntu2204 \\\n  --size Standard_B2s \\\n  --admin-username azureuser \\\n  --generate-ssh-keys</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0091","card":"q-az-900-014-4-service-types-iaas-paas-saas","sec":"az-900-s012","q":"Which Azure CLI command runs an OS update on an IaaS VM from outside it?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az vm run-command invoke \\\n  --resource-group myIaaSRG \\\n  --name myIaaSVM \\\n  --command-id RunShellScript \\\n  --scripts &quot;sudo apt update &amp;&amp; sudo apt upgrade -y&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0092","card":"q-az-900-014-4-service-types-iaas-paas-saas","sec":"az-900-s012","q":"Which Azure CLI commands install nginx on an IaaS VM and open port 80?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az vm run-command invoke \\\n  --resource-group myIaaSRG \\\n  --name myIaaSVM \\\n  --command-id RunShellScript \\\n  --scripts &quot;sudo apt install -y nginx&quot;\n\naz vm open-port --resource-group myIaaSRG --name myIaaSVM --port 80</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0093","card":"q-az-900-015-4-service-types-iaas-paas-saas","sec":"az-900-s012","q":"Which Python SDK call creates an IaaS VM?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>compute.virtual_machines.begin_create_or_update(&quot;myIaaSRG&quot;, &quot;myIaaSVM&quot;, vm_params)</code></pre></div>\n<p><code>vm_params</code> is a <code>VirtualMachine</code> built with <code>HardwareProfile(vm_size=\"Standard_B2s\")</code>, a <code>StorageProfile</code>, an <code>OSProfile</code> and a <code>NetworkProfile</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0094","card":"q-az-900-015-4-service-types-iaas-paas-saas","sec":"az-900-s012","q":"In the Python SDK VM example, which image does the <code>StorageProfile</code> reference?","a":"<p>Canonical Ubuntu: publisher <code>Canonical</code>, offer <code>0001-com-ubuntu-server-jammy</code>, sku <code>22_04-lts</code>, version <code>latest</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0095","card":"q-az-900-015-4-service-types-iaas-paas-saas","sec":"az-900-s012","q":"What turnkey features does PaaS App Service give you?","a":"<p>No OS management, and turnkey autoscale, custom domain, SSL and CI from GitHub.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0096","card":"q-az-900-015-4-service-types-iaas-paas-saas","sec":"az-900-s012","q":"Which Azure CLI commands create an App Service Plan and a Python web app?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az appservice plan create \\\n  --name myPlan \\\n  --resource-group myPaaSRG \\\n  --sku B1 \\\n  --is-linux\n\naz webapp create \\\n  --resource-group myPaaSRG \\\n  --plan myPlan \\\n  --name myPaaSWebApp \\\n  --runtime &quot;PYTHON:3.11&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0097","card":"q-az-900-015-4-service-types-iaas-paas-saas","sec":"az-900-s012","q":"Which Azure CLI command deploys code directly from a local folder to a web app?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az webapp up \\\n  --resource-group myPaaSRG \\\n  --name myPaaSWebApp \\\n  --runtime &quot;PYTHON:3.11&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0098","card":"q-az-900-016-4-service-types-iaas-paas-saas","sec":"az-900-s012","q":"Which Azure CLI command enables autoscaling on an App Service Plan with 1 to 5 instances?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az monitor autoscale create \\\n  --resource-group myPaaSRG \\\n  --resource myPlan \\\n  --resource-type Microsoft.Web/serverfarms \\\n  --name myAutoScale \\\n  --min-count 1 --max-count 5 --count 1</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0099","card":"q-az-900-016-4-service-types-iaas-paas-saas","sec":"az-900-s012","q":"Which Azure CLI command adds a custom domain to a web app?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az webapp config hostname add \\\n  --resource-group myPaaSRG \\\n  --webapp-name myPaaSWebApp \\\n  --hostname www.mysite.com</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0100","card":"q-az-900-016-4-service-types-iaas-paas-saas","sec":"az-900-s012","q":"Which Azure CLI command binds an SSL certificate to a web app?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az webapp config ssl bind \\\n  --resource-group myPaaSRG \\\n  --name myPaaSWebApp \\\n  --certificate-thumbprint &lt;thumbprint&gt; \\\n  --ssl-type SNI</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0101","card":"q-az-900-016-4-service-types-iaas-paas-saas","sec":"az-900-s012","q":"Which Azure CLI command sets up continuous deployment from GitHub to a web app?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az webapp deployment source config \\\n  --resource-group myPaaSRG \\\n  --name myPaaSWebApp \\\n  --repo-url https://github.com/user/repo \\\n  --branch main</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0102","card":"q-az-900-016-4-service-types-iaas-paas-saas","sec":"az-900-s012","q":"How do you work with SaaS such as Microsoft 365 programmatically?","a":"<p>You do not deploy or manage anything. You call the service's API (for example Microsoft Graph) or use web interfaces.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0103","card":"q-az-900-016-4-service-types-iaas-paas-saas","sec":"az-900-s012","q":"Which curl calls to Microsoft Graph get the current user's profile and list their emails?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>curl -H &quot;Authorization: Bearer &lt;access-token&gt;&quot; \\\n  https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/me\n\ncurl -H &quot;Authorization: Bearer &lt;access-token&gt;&quot; \\\n  https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/me/messages</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0104","card":"q-az-900-017-thought-experiment-choosing-a-cloud-mode","sec":"az-900-s013","q":"In the AZ-900 thought experiment, what requirements did Cora's boss Samuel give for choosing a cloud type?","a":"<p>VMs plus a database, no complex networking (too few network technicians), fault tolerance and reliability, always available including end-of-month demand spikes, <strong>privacy first</strong> (data must never sit on a network shared with an unknown company, and any shared party must be vetted for compliance), and a generous budget.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0105","card":"q-az-900-017-thought-experiment-choosing-a-cloud-mode","sec":"az-900-s013","q":"In the Cora thought experiment, why was public cloud rejected?","a":"<p>Shared infrastructure breaks the privacy requirement.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0106","card":"q-az-900-017-thought-experiment-choosing-a-cloud-mode","sec":"az-900-s013","q":"In the Cora thought experiment, why was hybrid cloud rejected?","a":"<p>It needs complex on-prem-to-cloud networking, and public VMs may fail compliance.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0107","card":"q-az-900-017-thought-experiment-choosing-a-cloud-mode","sec":"az-900-s013","q":"In the Cora thought experiment, which model won and why?","a":"<p><strong>Private cloud with a third-party provider</strong>. It is single-tenant, the provider handles networking, the provider can be vetted, scaling and fault tolerance are available, and the higher cost is acceptable.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0108","card":"q-az-900-017-thought-experiment-choosing-a-cloud-mode","sec":"az-900-s013","q":"What is the lesson of the cloud-model thought experiment?","a":"<p>List requirements first, then test each model against them. Privacy and compliance push toward private cloud even at higher cost.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0109","card":"q-az-900-017-thought-experiment-choosing-a-cloud-mode","sec":"az-900-s013","q":"What is Azure's private-cloud offering?","a":"<p>Azure Stack HCI. It runs Azure services on your own hardware (or the provider's dedicated hardware) and uses the same CLI.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0110","card":"q-az-900-018-geographies-regions-region-pairs","sec":"az-900-s014","q":"What is an Azure geography?","a":"<p>A boundary defined by country, continent or regulation, so data stays compliant with local rules.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0111","card":"q-az-900-018-geographies-regions-region-pairs","sec":"az-900-s014","q":"What is an Azure region?","a":"<p>A physical location within a geography that contains data centers and the facilities Azure needs.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0112","card":"q-az-900-018-geographies-regions-region-pairs","sec":"az-900-s014","q":"What is an Azure region pair?","a":"<p>Each region is paired with another, at least about 300 miles apart, for disaster recovery.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0113","card":"q-az-900-018-geographies-regions-region-pairs","sec":"az-900-s014","q":"What happens to your resources when an Azure region fails and you replicated to its pair?","a":"<p>Automatic failover to the paired region.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0114","card":"q-az-900-018-geographies-regions-region-pairs","sec":"az-900-s014","q":"What are rolling updates in Azure region pairs?","a":"<p>Microsoft updates one region of a pair, verifies it, then updates the other, so Azure updates cause no downtime.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0115","card":"q-az-900-018-geographies-regions-region-pairs","sec":"az-900-s014","q":"Which Azure CLI commands list all regions and show details of one region?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az account list-locations --output table\n\naz account list-locations --query &quot;[?name==&#x27;eastus&#x27;]&quot; --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0116","card":"q-az-900-018-geographies-regions-region-pairs","sec":"az-900-s014","q":"Which Azure CLI command creates geo-redundant storage that replicates to the paired region?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az storage account create \\\n  --name mygrsaccount \\\n  --resource-group myPrimaryRG \\\n  --location eastus \\\n  --sku Standard_GRS</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0117","card":"q-az-900-018-geographies-regions-region-pairs","sec":"az-900-s014","q":"Which Python SDK loop prints each Azure region and its paired region?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>for location in client.subscriptions.list_locations(&quot;&lt;subscription-id&gt;&quot;):\n    paired = location.metadata.paired_region\n    pair_name = paired[0].name if paired else &quot;None&quot;\n    print(f&quot;{location.name} ↔ {pair_name}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0118","card":"q-az-900-019-sovereign-regions","sec":"az-900-s015","q":"What are Azure sovereign regions?","a":"<p>Regions that are completely isolated: separate portals, endpoints and operators.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0119","card":"q-az-900-019-sovereign-regions","sec":"az-900-s015","q":"What is Azure Government (US)?","a":"<p>A sovereign region where data stays in the US and only screened US citizens operate it. It is separate from public Azure with dedicated networking, and a DoD subset has dedicated data centers. It is for US government, cities and municipalities with governmental affiliation.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0120","card":"q-az-900-019-sovereign-regions","sec":"az-900-s015","q":"What is Azure Germany, and who operates it?","a":"<p>A sovereign region that follows GDPR and EU rules, available to EU, European Free Trade Association members and the UK. <strong>T-Systems International</strong> operates it as data trustee with full control of data and infrastructure. Microsoft only manages systems that have no access to customer data.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0121","card":"q-az-900-019-sovereign-regions","sec":"az-900-s015","q":"What is Azure China, and who operates it?","a":"<p>A sovereign region operated by <strong>Shanghai Blue Cloud Technology</strong> (owned by 21Vianet). It complies with China's regulations.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0122","card":"q-az-900-019-sovereign-regions","sec":"az-900-s015","q":"Which Azure CLI commands switch to the Azure Government cloud and list its regions?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az cloud set --name AzureUSGovernment\naz login\naz account list-locations --output table  # Shows government-only regions</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0123","card":"q-az-900-019-sovereign-regions","sec":"az-900-s015","q":"Which Azure CLI commands switch to the Azure China cloud?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az cloud set --name AzureChinaCloud\naz login</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0124","card":"q-az-900-020-availability-zones","sec":"az-900-s016","q":"What is an Azure availability zone?","a":"<p>A unique physical location <strong>within a region</strong>, with one or more data centers. Zone-enabled regions have <strong>at least 3 zones</strong>, and not every region supports zones.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0125","card":"q-az-900-020-availability-zones","sec":"az-900-s016","q":"What is the difference between zonal and zone-redundant services?","a":"<p>With a <strong>zonal</strong> service you choose the zones (example: Virtual Machines). With a <strong>zone-redundant</strong> service Azure replicates automatically (example: Azure Storage).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0126","card":"q-az-900-020-availability-zones","sec":"az-900-s016","q":"Do availability zones give fault tolerance or disaster recovery?","a":"<p>Fault tolerance, not disaster recovery. All zones sit in one region, so a regional disaster can take them all. Use region pairs for DR.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0127","card":"q-az-900-020-availability-zones","sec":"az-900-s016","q":"Which Azure CLI command deploys a VM to availability zone 1?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az vm create --resource-group myRG --name myVM-Z1 --image Ubuntu2204 --zone 1 --size Standard_B2s --generate-ssh-keys</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0128","card":"q-az-900-020-availability-zones","sec":"az-900-s016","q":"Which Azure CLI command creates zone-redundant storage?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az storage account create \\\n  --name myzoneredundant \\\n  --resource-group myRG \\\n  --location eastus \\\n  --sku Standard_ZRS   # Zone-Redundant Storage</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0129","card":"q-az-900-020-availability-zones","sec":"az-900-s016","q":"Which Azure CLI command lists availability zones for a region?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az vm list-skus --location eastus --zone --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0130","card":"q-az-900-021-data-centers","sec":"az-900-s017","q":"What is an Azure data center?","a":"<p>A physical building in a region. Each region has at least 2.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0131","card":"q-az-900-021-data-centers","sec":"az-900-s017","q":"What does each Azure data center have of its own?","a":"<p>Its own climate control, power supply and generators, and network gear.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0132","card":"q-az-900-021-data-centers","sec":"az-900-s017","q":"Who owns the cables between Azure data centers?","a":"<p>The cables are owned or leased exclusively by Microsoft.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0133","card":"q-az-900-021-data-centers","sec":"az-900-s017","q":"Why does one Azure data center failing not affect the others?","a":"<p>None depends on another's power or water.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0134","card":"q-az-900-022-resources-resource-groups-management-gro","sec":"az-900-s018","q":"What is an Azure resource?","a":"<p>Any entity you create (VM, web app, database, storage).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0135","card":"q-az-900-022-resources-resource-groups-management-gro","sec":"az-900-s018","q":"What is an Azure resource group (RG)?","a":"<p>A logical container. Every resource is in <strong>exactly one</strong> RG.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0136","card":"q-az-900-022-resources-resource-groups-management-gro","sec":"az-900-s018","q":"What are the benefits of Azure resource groups?","a":"<p>A per-group cost view, deleting the group deletes everything in it, you can tag the group and filter invoices by tag, and you can export it as an ARM template to redeploy elsewhere.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0137","card":"q-az-900-022-resources-resource-groups-management-gro","sec":"az-900-s018","q":"What is an Azure management group, and what can it contain?","a":"<p>A group that organizes <strong>subscriptions</strong>. It can contain subscriptions and other (nested) management groups, but not resource groups or resources.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0138","card":"q-az-900-022-resources-resource-groups-management-gro","sec":"az-900-s018","q":"What is the Azure resource hierarchy from top to bottom?","a":"<p>Management groups, then subscriptions, then resource groups, then resources. You organize by department, project or environment as you like.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0139","card":"q-az-900-022-resources-resource-groups-management-gro","sec":"az-900-s018","q":"Which Azure CLI command tags a resource group for billing?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az group update --name myProjectRG --tags Department=Training Project=AZ900</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0140","card":"q-az-900-022-resources-resource-groups-management-gro","sec":"az-900-s018","q":"Which Azure CLI commands list all resources in a resource group and delete everything in it in one step?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az resource list --resource-group myProjectRG --output table\n\naz group delete --name myProjectRG --yes --no-wait</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0141","card":"q-az-900-022-resources-resource-groups-management-gro","sec":"az-900-s018","q":"Which Azure CLI command exports a resource group as an ARM template?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az group export --name myProjectRG &gt; myProjectRG-template.json</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0142","card":"q-az-900-022-resources-resource-groups-management-gro","sec":"az-900-s018","q":"Which Python SDK calls create, list and delete resource groups?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>client.resource_groups.create_or_update(&quot;myProjectRG&quot;, {&quot;location&quot;: &quot;eastus&quot;, &quot;tags&quot;: {&quot;Department&quot;: &quot;Training&quot;}})\n\nfor rg in client.resource_groups.list():\n    print(f&quot;{rg.name} ({rg.location}) - Tags: {rg.tags}&quot;)\n\nclient.resource_groups.begin_delete(&quot;myProjectRG&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0143","card":"q-az-900-022-resources-resource-groups-management-gro","sec":"az-900-s018","q":"Which Azure CLI commands create a management group and a nested management group under it?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az account management-group create --name SalesDept --display-name &quot;Sales Department&quot;\n\naz account management-group create --name DevTeam --display-name &quot;Dev Team&quot; --parent SalesDept</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0144","card":"q-az-900-022-resources-resource-groups-management-gro","sec":"az-900-s018","q":"Which Azure CLI command moves a subscription into a management group?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az account management-group subscription add \\\n  --name SalesDept \\\n  --subscription &quot;&lt;subscription-id&gt;&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0145","card":"q-az-900-022-resources-resource-groups-management-gro","sec":"az-900-s018","q":"Which Azure CLI commands list management groups and show the hierarchy?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az account management-group list --output table\n\naz account management-group show --name SalesDept --expand --recurse</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0146","card":"q-az-900-023-6-compute-and-networking","sec":"az-900-s019","q":"What is compute in Azure?","a":"<p>Any service that consumes CPU and memory.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0147","card":"q-az-900-024-containers","sec":"az-900-s020","q":"What is a container?","a":"<p>An isolated environment where an app and its dependencies run.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0148","card":"q-az-900-024-containers","sec":"az-900-s020","q":"What are the three steps in how a container runs?","a":"<ol>\n  <li>It is built from an <strong>image</strong> (like a zip of OS pieces, code, modules, web servers).</li>\n  <li>Images live in a <strong>repository</strong>.</li>\n  <li>A <strong>container runtime</strong> (Docker) downloads and runs the image.</li>\n</ol>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0149","card":"q-az-900-024-containers","sec":"az-900-s020","q":"Why does a Linux container image need a Linux host?","a":"<p>Containers hold only <strong>user-mode</strong> OS components and rely on the host's <strong>kernel</strong>. A Linux image needs a Linux host, and a Windows image needs a Windows host.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0150","card":"q-az-900-024-containers","sec":"az-900-s020","q":"Which Docker commands pull and run the ASP.NET sample image?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>docker pull mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/samples:aspnetapp\ndocker run -d -p 8080:8080 mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/samples:aspnetapp</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0151","card":"q-az-900-025-compute-types","sec":"az-900-s021","q":"How do Virtual Machines, Container Instances (ACI) and Functions compare by service model?","a":"<p>VMs are IaaS, ACI is PaaS, and Functions is serverless.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0152","card":"q-az-900-025-compute-types","sec":"az-900-s021","q":"What do you manage in a VM, in ACI and in Azure Functions?","a":"<p>VMs: OS, runtime and app. ACI: app and image. Functions: code only.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0153","card":"q-az-900-025-compute-types","sec":"az-900-s021","q":"What is each of VMs, ACI and Functions best for?","a":"<p>VMs: full control and lift-and-shift. ACI: small, quick container workloads. Functions: event-driven microservices.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0154","card":"q-az-900-025-compute-types","sec":"az-900-s021","q":"How is each of VMs, ACI and Functions billed?","a":"<p>VMs: by VM uptime. ACI: by CPU and memory used. Functions: per execution.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0155","card":"q-az-900-025-compute-types","sec":"az-900-s021","q":"What are Azure VMs?","a":"<p>Windows or Linux machines in many sizes. Azure installs the OS and you configure everything else.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0156","card":"q-az-900-025-compute-types","sec":"az-900-s021","q":"What is Azure Container Instances (ACI), and when do you use AKS instead?","a":"<p>ACI runs containers without VMs, with <strong>container groups</strong> for several containers in one instance. For heavy or long-running workloads use <strong>AKS</strong>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0157","card":"q-az-900-025-compute-types","sec":"az-900-s021","q":"What are Azure Functions?","a":"<p>Microservices that take an input, do an operation and return a result. They are <strong>event-driven</strong> (file upload, HTTP request, timer), billed by consumption, with no VM costs.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0158","card":"q-az-900-025-compute-types","sec":"az-900-s021","q":"Which Azure CLI commands create a VM and open port 80?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az vm create \\\n  --resource-group myResourceGroup \\\n  --name myVM \\\n  --image Ubuntu2204 \\\n  --admin-username azureuser \\\n  --generate-ssh-keys\n\naz vm open-port --port 80 --resource-group myResourceGroup --name myVM</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0159","card":"q-az-900-025-compute-types","sec":"az-900-s021","q":"Which Azure CLI commands deploy a container with ACI and check its state?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az container create \\\n  --resource-group myResourceGroup \\\n  --name mycontainer \\\n  --image mcr.microsoft.com/azuredocs/aci-helloworld \\\n  --ports 80 \\\n  --dns-name-label my-aci-demo\n\naz container show --resource-group myResourceGroup --name mycontainer --query instanceView.state</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0160","card":"q-az-900-025-compute-types","sec":"az-900-s021","q":"What does an Azure Function in Python with an HTTP trigger on route <code>hello</code> look like?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.route(route=&quot;hello&quot;)\ndef hello(req: func.HttpRequest) -&gt; func.HttpResponse:\n    name = req.params.get(&#x27;name&#x27;, &#x27;World&#x27;)\n    logging.info(f&quot;HTTP trigger processed a request for {name}&quot;)\n    return func.HttpResponse(f&quot;Hello, {name}!&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0161","card":"q-az-900-025-compute-types","sec":"az-900-s021","q":"Which commands create and publish an Azure Function project with an HTTP trigger?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>func init MyFunctionProject --python\ncd MyFunctionProject\nfunc new --name hello --template &quot;HTTP trigger&quot;\nfunc azure functionapp publish myFunctionApp</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0162","card":"q-az-900-026-vm-options","sec":"az-900-s022","q":"Where does an Azure VM run?","a":"<p>Each VM is a guest on a host server in an Azure data center.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0163","card":"q-az-900-026-vm-options","sec":"az-900-s022","q":"Does stopping (deallocating) an Azure VM stop billing?","a":"<p>Yes. Deallocating a VM stops billing, and starting it resumes billing.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0164","card":"q-az-900-026-vm-options","sec":"az-900-s022","q":"Which Azure CLI commands deallocate a VM and start it again?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az vm deallocate --resource-group AZ900 --name VM1\n\naz vm start --resource-group AZ900 --name VM1</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0165","card":"q-az-900-026-vm-options","sec":"az-900-s022","q":"What is an Azure availability set, and how does it differ from availability zones?","a":"<p>An availability set gives high availability inside a data center. It is not the same as availability zones.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0166","card":"q-az-900-026-vm-options","sec":"az-900-s022","q":"What are fault domains and update domains in an availability set?","a":"<p>A <strong>fault domain</strong> is a logical physical server rack and protects against rack failures. <strong>Update domains</strong>: Azure reboots one update domain at a time and waits for VMs to return before the next.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0167","card":"q-az-900-026-vm-options","sec":"az-900-s022","q":"Which Azure CLI command creates an availability set with 2 fault domains and 3 update domains?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az vm availability-set create \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --name myAvailabilitySet \\\n  --platform-fault-domain-count 2 \\\n  --platform-update-domain-count 3</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0168","card":"q-az-900-026-vm-options","sec":"az-900-s022","q":"Which Azure CLI command creates a VM inside an availability set?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az vm create \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --name VM1 \\\n  --image Ubuntu2204 \\\n  --availability-set myAvailabilitySet \\\n  --admin-username azureuser \\\n  --generate-ssh-keys</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0169","card":"q-az-900-026-vm-options","sec":"az-900-s022","q":"What are Azure VM Scale Sets (VMSS)?","a":"<p>They automatically scale a group of identical VMs using autoscale, deployed with availability sets for fault tolerance.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0170","card":"q-az-900-026-vm-options","sec":"az-900-s022","q":"What is Azure Virtual Desktop?","a":"<p>Desktop virtualization in the cloud. You run apps without local installation. Clients exist for Windows, macOS, iOS, iPadOS, Android and web browsers, and each user gets their own profile.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0171","card":"q-az-900-027-resources-created-with-a-vm","sec":"az-900-s023","q":"Which resources does Azure create with a VM?","a":"<p>A virtual network, the VM, a public IP address, a network security group (firewall rules), a network interface, an OS disk, and an SSH key (Linux, if SSH is chosen).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0172","card":"q-az-900-027-resources-created-with-a-vm","sec":"az-900-s023","q":"Why keep all the resources of a VM in one resource group?","a":"<p>Cleanup becomes a single delete.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0173","card":"q-az-900-027-resources-created-with-a-vm","sec":"az-900-s023","q":"Which Azure CLI command lists all resources in a resource group, and which deletes the group and all its resources?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az resource list --resource-group AZ900 --output table\n\naz group delete --name AZ900 --yes --no-wait</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0174","card":"q-az-900-028-application-hosting","sec":"az-900-s024","q":"What is Azure App Service, and what is an App Service Plan?","a":"<p>App Service (PaaS) runs web apps in the cloud. Apps run on VMs in an <strong>App Service Plan</strong>, the unit of scaling. All apps in the plan share the same VMs.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0175","card":"q-az-900-028-application-hosting","sec":"az-900-s024","q":"How do plan tiers differ in App Service?","a":"<p>Lower plan tiers cost less with fewer features. Higher tiers add power and features.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0176","card":"q-az-900-028-application-hosting","sec":"az-900-s024","q":"What naming rule applies to App Service app names?","a":"<p>They must be <strong>globally unique</strong> (<code>&lt;app-name&gt;.azurewebsites.net</code>).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0177","card":"q-az-900-028-application-hosting","sec":"az-900-s024","q":"How can you scale an App Service plan?","a":"<p>Scaling applies to the whole plan: <strong>scale up</strong> (bigger VM), <strong>scale out</strong> (more instances) or <strong>autoscale</strong> by metric (CPU, traffic).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0178","card":"q-az-900-028-application-hosting","sec":"az-900-s024","q":"What turnkey authentication does App Service offer?","a":"<p>You can add Microsoft, Apple, Facebook, GitHub or Google sign-in with no auth code.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0179","card":"q-az-900-028-application-hosting","sec":"az-900-s024","q":"Which Azure CLI commands create an App Service Plan with the S1 SKU and a web app on it?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az appservice plan create \\\n  --name JonesASP \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --sku S1\n\naz webapp create \\\n  --name az900wa \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --plan JonesASP \\\n  --runtime &quot;DOTNET|4.8&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0180","card":"q-az-900-028-application-hosting","sec":"az-900-s024","q":"Which Azure CLI command scales an App Service Plan up to the S2 tier?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az appservice plan update --name JonesASP --resource-group AZ900 --sku S2</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0181","card":"q-az-900-028-application-hosting","sec":"az-900-s024","q":"Which Azure CLI command scales a web app out to 3 instances?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az webapp scale --name az900wa --resource-group AZ900 --instance-count 3</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0182","card":"q-az-900-028-application-hosting","sec":"az-900-s024","q":"Which Azure CLI command enables autoscale on an App Service Plan?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az monitor autoscale create \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --resource JonesASP \\\n  --resource-type Microsoft.Web/serverfarms \\\n  --min-count 1 \\\n  --max-count 5 \\\n  --count 1</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0183","card":"q-az-900-028-application-hosting","sec":"az-900-s024","q":"Which Azure CLI command scales out an App Service Plan when CPU is above 70%?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az monitor autoscale rule create \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --autoscale-name autoscale \\\n  --condition &quot;CpuPercentage &gt; 70 avg 5m&quot; \\\n  --scale out 1</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0184","card":"q-az-900-028-application-hosting","sec":"az-900-s024","q":"Which Azure CLI command enables the Microsoft identity provider on a web app?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az webapp auth microsoft update \\\n  --name az900wa \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --client-id &lt;app-client-id&gt; \\\n  --client-secret &lt;app-client-secret&gt; \\\n  --issuer &quot;https://login.microsoftonline.com/&lt;tenant-id&gt;/v2.0&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0185","card":"q-az-900-029-application-hosting","sec":"az-900-s024","q":"What is Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS)?","a":"<p>Managed <strong>container orchestration</strong>, good at scaling containers and keeping them available. You pay only for the compute in the cluster.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0186","card":"q-az-900-029-application-hosting","sec":"az-900-s024","q":"What are the control plane and nodes in an AKS Kubernetes cluster?","a":"<p>The <strong>control plane</strong> manages scaling in and out. The <strong>nodes</strong> run containers.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0187","card":"q-az-900-029-application-hosting","sec":"az-900-s024","q":"Which Azure CLI commands create an AKS cluster with 2 nodes and get credentials for it?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az aks create \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --name myAKSCluster \\\n  --node-count 2 \\\n  --generate-ssh-keys\n\naz aks get-credentials --resource-group AZ900 --name myAKSCluster</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0188","card":"q-az-900-029-application-hosting","sec":"az-900-s024","q":"Which kubectl commands deploy an app with 3 replicas and expose it with a load balancer?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kubectl create deployment myapp --image=mcr.microsoft.com/azuredocs/aci-helloworld --replicas=3\n\nkubectl expose deployment myapp --type=LoadBalancer --port=80 --target-port=8080</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0189","card":"q-az-900-029-application-hosting","sec":"az-900-s024","q":"Why are Azure Virtual Machines the most flexible hosting option?","a":"<p>They give full control, but also the most responsibility: you install, configure and secure everything.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0190","card":"q-az-900-029-application-hosting","sec":"az-900-s024","q":"How do App Service, AKS and VMs compare on flexibility?","a":"<p>App Service: supported runtimes only. AKS: high. VMs: full control.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0191","card":"q-az-900-029-application-hosting","sec":"az-900-s024","q":"How do App Service, AKS and VMs compare on responsibility and scaling?","a":"<p>Responsibility: App Service low, AKS medium (containers), VMs high. Scaling: App Service has built-in up/out/autoscale, AKS uses container orchestration, VMs scale manually or with VMSS.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0192","card":"q-az-900-029-application-hosting","sec":"az-900-s024","q":"What is each of App Service, AKS and VMs best for, and what is turnkey in each?","a":"<p>App Service: web apps and APIs, with turnkey auth, SSL and deployment slots. AKS: microservices and containers, with a managed control plane. VMs: lift-and-shift and custom environments, with no turnkey features.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0193","card":"q-az-900-030-virtual-networking","sec":"az-900-s025","q":"What is an Azure VNet?","a":"<p>Your own network in Azure with an <strong>IP address space in CIDR</strong> (for example <code>10.0.0.0/16</code>, 65,534 usable IPs), split into <strong>subnets</strong>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0194","card":"q-az-900-030-virtual-networking","sec":"az-900-s025","q":"What is a typical multi-tier VNet layout, and which tier faces the internet?","a":"<p>A web tier (internet-facing), a middle tier (business rules) and a data tier (no direct internet). Only the web tier should face the internet, and the web tier should not talk straight to the data tier.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0195","card":"q-az-900-030-virtual-networking","sec":"az-900-s025","q":"Which Azure CLI commands create a VNet and a WebTier subnet?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az network vnet create \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --name myVNet \\\n  --address-prefix 10.0.0.0/16\n\naz network vnet subnet create \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 --vnet-name myVNet \\\n  --name WebTier --address-prefix 10.0.1.0/24</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0196","card":"q-az-900-030-virtual-networking","sec":"az-900-s025","q":"Which Azure CLI commands create the MiddleTier and DataTier subnets in a VNet?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az network vnet subnet create \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 --vnet-name myVNet \\\n  --name MiddleTier --address-prefix 10.0.2.0/24\naz network vnet subnet create \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 --vnet-name myVNet \\\n  --name DataTier --address-prefix 10.0.3.0/24</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0197","card":"q-az-900-030-virtual-networking","sec":"az-900-s025","q":"Which Azure CLI command lists the subnets of a VNet?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az network vnet subnet list --resource-group AZ900 --vnet-name myVNet --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0198","card":"q-az-900-030-virtual-networking","sec":"az-900-s025","q":"What is Azure VNet peering?","a":"<p>It connects two VNets over <strong>Microsoft's private backbone</strong>, not the internet. It works in the same region or different regions (Global VNet Peering). Peered traffic is <strong>not encrypted</strong>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0199","card":"q-az-900-030-virtual-networking","sec":"az-900-s025","q":"Which Azure CLI commands create the peering from VNet1 to VNet2?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az network vnet peering create \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 --vnet-name VNet1 \\\n  --name VNet1-to-VNet2 --remote-vnet $VNET2_ID --allow-vnet-access</code></pre></div>\n<p>Create the peering in both directions, so VNet2 also needs a peering to VNet1.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0200","card":"q-az-900-030-virtual-networking","sec":"az-900-s025","q":"What is Azure DNS, and how do public and private zones differ?","a":"<p>Azure DNS hosts DNS records (A, CNAME, MX...). <strong>Public zones</strong> are internet-facing. <strong>Private zones</strong> only resolve inside Azure VNets.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0201","card":"q-az-900-030-virtual-networking","sec":"az-900-s025","q":"Which Azure CLI commands create a public DNS zone and add an A record?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az network dns zone create --resource-group AZ900 --name example.com\n\naz network dns record-set a add-record \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 --zone-name example.com \\\n  --record-set-name www --ipv4-address 10.0.1.4</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0202","card":"q-az-900-030-virtual-networking","sec":"az-900-s025","q":"Which Azure CLI commands create a private DNS zone and link it to a VNet?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az network private-dns zone create --resource-group AZ900 --name private.example.com\n\naz network private-dns link vnet create \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 --zone-name private.example.com \\\n  --name myLink --virtual-network myVNet --registration-enabled true</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0203","card":"q-az-900-031-virtual-networking","sec":"az-900-s025","q":"What is Azure VPN Gateway, and what is its maximum speed?","a":"<p>It provides encrypted connections between Azure VNets and other networks. Azure creates a managed gateway subnet with 2+ VMs (not accessible to you). The maximum is <strong>1.25 Gbps</strong>, and encryption adds overhead.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0204","card":"q-az-900-031-virtual-networking","sec":"az-900-s025","q":"What are the Azure VPN Gateway connection types?","a":"<p><strong>VNet-to-VNet</strong> connects two Azure VNets. <strong>Site-to-Site</strong> connects an Azure VNet and an on-prem network. <strong>Point-to-Site</strong> connects one device (phone, laptop) and an Azure VNet.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0205","card":"q-az-900-031-virtual-networking","sec":"az-900-s025","q":"Which Azure CLI commands create the gateway subnet and a static public IP for a VPN gateway?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az network vnet subnet create \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 --vnet-name myVNet \\\n  --name GatewaySubnet --address-prefix 10.0.255.0/27\n\naz network public-ip create \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 --name myGatewayIP --allocation-method Static</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0206","card":"q-az-900-031-virtual-networking","sec":"az-900-s025","q":"Which Azure CLI command creates a VPN gateway, and how long does it take?","a":"<p>It takes about 30 minutes.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az network vnet-gateway create \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 --name myVPNGateway \\\n  --vnet myVNet --public-ip-addresses myGatewayIP \\\n  --gateway-type Vpn --vpn-type RouteBased --sku VpnGw1</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0207","card":"q-az-900-031-virtual-networking","sec":"az-900-s025","q":"When do you use VNet peering and when VPN Gateway to connect two networks?","a":"<p>For two Azure VNets, peering is faster (no encryption overhead, no 1.25 Gbps cap). Use VPN Gateway when you need encryption or a non-Azure network.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0208","card":"q-az-900-031-virtual-networking","sec":"az-900-s025","q":"What is Azure ExpressRoute?","a":"<p>Dedicated private connectivity from on-prem to Azure. <strong>Traffic never crosses the internet.</strong> The connection is a <strong>circuit</strong>: you, a third-party provider (usually an ISP), Microsoft Enterprise Edge (MSEE), then Azure.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0209","card":"q-az-900-031-virtual-networking","sec":"az-900-s025","q":"How do VPN Gateway and ExpressRoute compare on speed, path and provider?","a":"<p>VPN Gateway: up to 1.25 Gbps, over the internet (encrypted), no provider. ExpressRoute: up to 10 Gbps (100 Gbps with ExpressRoute Direct), over dedicated fiber via MSEE, with a third-party provider.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0210","card":"q-az-900-032-public-vs-private-endpoints","sec":"az-900-s026","q":"What are public and private endpoints in Azure?","a":"<p>A <strong>public endpoint</strong> is an IP reachable over the internet. A <strong>private endpoint</strong> is an IP reachable only on a private network.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0211","card":"q-az-900-032-public-vs-private-endpoints","sec":"az-900-s026","q":"Can an Azure resource have both a public and a private endpoint?","a":"<p>Yes. A VM has a private IP from its VNet and a public IP resource.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0212","card":"q-az-900-032-public-vs-private-endpoints","sec":"az-900-s026","q":"Which Azure CLI command shows a VM's public and private IPs?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az vm show \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 --name VM1 \\\n  --show-details \\\n  --query &#x27;{Name:name, PrivateIP:privateIps, PublicIP:publicIps}&#x27; -o table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0213","card":"q-az-900-033-storage-services","sec":"az-900-s027","q":"What do Azure Blob Storage, Azure Disks and Azure Files store, and how are they accessed?","a":"<p>Blob Storage: unstructured files (blobs) in containers, via REST API, CLI and SDKs. Azure Disks: managed HDD/SSD disks, attached to VMs. Azure Files: SMB file shares, mounted as <code>//server/share</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0214","card":"q-az-900-033-storage-services","sec":"az-900-s027","q":"What is each of Blob Storage, Azure Disks and Azure Files best for?","a":"<p>Blob Storage: images, video, documents, logs and VHDs. Azure Disks: OS disks and persistent data disks. Azure Files: shared files and lift-and-shift file servers.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0215","card":"q-az-900-033-storage-services","sec":"az-900-s027","q":"What are the Azure blob types and their use?","a":"<p>Block blobs: general files (images, video, documents). Append blobs: append-only data such as logs. Page blobs: VHDs used by VMs.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0216","card":"q-az-900-033-storage-services","sec":"az-900-s027","q":"Which Azure CLI command creates a storage account with locally redundant storage?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az storage account create \\\n  --name az900storage \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --location centralus \\\n  --sku Standard_LRS</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0217","card":"q-az-900-033-storage-services","sec":"az-900-s027","q":"Which Azure CLI commands create a blob container and upload a block blob?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az storage container create \\\n  --name mycontainer \\\n  --account-name az900storage\n\naz storage blob upload \\\n  --account-name az900storage \\\n  --container-name mycontainer \\\n  --name photo.jpg \\\n  --file ./photo.jpg</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0218","card":"q-az-900-033-storage-services","sec":"az-900-s027","q":"Which flag uploads an append blob with <code>az storage blob upload</code>?","a":"<p><code>--type append</code>, for example:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az storage blob upload \\\n  --account-name az900storage \\\n  --container-name mycontainer \\\n  --name app.log \\\n  --file ./app.log \\\n  --type append</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0219","card":"q-az-900-033-storage-services","sec":"az-900-s027","q":"Which Azure CLI command lists the blobs in a container?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az storage blob list --account-name az900storage --container-name mycontainer --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0220","card":"q-az-900-034-storage-services","sec":"az-900-s027","q":"How do Azure Disks work with a VM?","a":"<p>Azure auto-creates the OS disk with a VM. For persistent data, add a separate <strong>data disk</strong>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0221","card":"q-az-900-034-storage-services","sec":"az-900-s027","q":"Which Azure CLI commands create a 128 GB SSD managed data disk and attach it to a VM?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az disk create \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --name myDataDisk \\\n  --size-gb 128 \\\n  --sku Premium_LRS\n\naz vm disk attach \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --vm-name VM1 \\\n  --name myDataDisk</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0222","card":"q-az-900-034-storage-services","sec":"az-900-s027","q":"Which Azure CLI command lists disks in a resource group?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az disk list --resource-group AZ900 --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0223","card":"q-az-900-034-storage-services","sec":"az-900-s027","q":"What is Azure File Sync, and why use it?","a":"<p>Azure Files SMB shares are mapped like a network drive and can be slow over the internet. <strong>Azure File Sync</strong> syncs files to an on-prem server for local speed while the data stays in Azure.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0224","card":"q-az-900-034-storage-services","sec":"az-900-s027","q":"Which Azure CLI commands create a 50 GB file share and upload a file to it?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az storage share create \\\n  --name myfileshare \\\n  --account-name az900storage \\\n  --quota 50\n\naz storage file upload \\\n  --share-name myfileshare \\\n  --account-name az900storage \\\n  --source ./report.pdf</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0225","card":"q-az-900-034-storage-services","sec":"az-900-s027","q":"Which Azure CLI command lists files in an Azure file share?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az storage file list --share-name myfileshare --account-name az900storage --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0226","card":"q-az-900-034-storage-services","sec":"az-900-s027","q":"Which Linux command mounts an Azure file share?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>sudo mount -t cifs \\\n  //az900storage.file.core.windows.net/myfileshare /mnt/myshare \\\n  -o vers=3.0,username=az900storage,password=&lt;storage-account-key&gt;,dir_mode=0777,file_mode=0777</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0227","card":"q-az-900-035-blob-access-tiers","sec":"az-900-s028","q":"In Azure Blob Storage, what does the cost of a blob consist of?","a":"<p>Storage used plus operations and transfers.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0228","card":"q-az-900-035-blob-access-tiers","sec":"az-900-s028","q":"Compare the Hot, Cool and Archive blob tiers on storage cost, access cost, minimum retention and use.","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Storage cost</th><th>Access cost</th><th>Minimum retention</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Hot</strong></td><td>Highest</td><td>Lowest</td><td>None</td><td>Frequently accessed</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Cool</strong></td><td>Lower</td><td>Higher</td><td>30 days</td><td>Infrequent, kept longer</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Archive</strong></td><td>Lowest</td><td>Highest</td><td>180 days</td><td>Long-term archive</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0229","card":"q-az-900-035-blob-access-tiers","sec":"az-900-s028","q":"What happens in Azure Blob Storage if you delete a blob, or move it to another tier, before the minimum retention of Cool or Archive?","a":"<p>You pay a prorated penalty.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0230","card":"q-az-900-035-blob-access-tiers","sec":"az-900-s028","q":"Why must an Archive blob be hydrated, and how fast is the first byte available?","a":"<p>Archive blobs must be hydrated (moved to Cool or Hot) before you can access them. The first byte is guaranteed within 15 hours, usually much faster.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0231","card":"q-az-900-035-blob-access-tiers","sec":"az-900-s028","q":"Which Azure CLI command uploads a blob to the Hot tier?","a":"<p>Use <code>az storage blob upload</code> with <code>--tier Hot</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az storage blob upload \\\n  --account-name az900storage \\\n  --container-name mycontainer \\\n  --name data.csv --file ./data.csv \\\n  --tier Hot</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0232","card":"q-az-900-035-blob-access-tiers","sec":"az-900-s028","q":"Which Azure CLI command moves an existing blob to the Cool tier?","a":"<p><code>az storage blob set-tier</code> with <code>--tier Cool</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az storage blob set-tier \\\n  --account-name az900storage \\\n  --container-name mycontainer \\\n  --name data.csv --tier Cool</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0233","card":"q-az-900-035-blob-access-tiers","sec":"az-900-s028","q":"How do you hydrate an Archive blob back to Hot with the Azure CLI?","a":"<p>Run <code>az storage blob set-tier</code> with <code>--tier Hot</code>. The same command with <code>--tier Archive</code> moves a blob to Archive.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az storage blob set-tier \\\n  --account-name az900storage \\\n  --container-name mycontainer \\\n  --name data.csv --tier Hot</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0234","card":"q-az-900-036-redundancy","sec":"az-900-s029","q":"What are the Azure storage redundancy options for a single primary region (fault tolerance, no DR)?","a":"<p>LRS and ZRS. Both keep 3 copies.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>LRS</strong>: all copies in the same data center. It is the least durable, and a data-center-wide failure loses data.</li>\n  <li><strong>ZRS</strong>: one copy per availability zone. It survives a single data center failure.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0235","card":"q-az-900-036-redundancy","sec":"az-900-s029","q":"What are the Azure storage redundancy options for multi-region disaster recovery?","a":"<p>GRS and GZRS.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>GRS</strong>: 3 LRS copies in the primary region (same data center) plus 3 LRS copies in a distant region.</li>\n  <li><strong>GZRS</strong>: 3 ZRS copies in the primary region (across zones) plus 3 LRS copies in a distant region.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0236","card":"q-az-900-036-redundancy","sec":"az-900-s029","q":"What is the difference between GRS and GZRS in Azure Storage?","a":"<p>The primary region. GRS keeps 3 copies in the same data center, GZRS keeps 3 copies across zones. Both add 3 LRS copies in a distant region.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0237","card":"q-az-900-036-redundancy","sec":"az-900-s029","q":"Which Azure CLI flag chooses the redundancy of a storage account, and how do you create a ZRS account?","a":"<p>The <code>--sku</code> flag, for example <code>Standard_ZRS</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az storage account create \\\n  --name az900zrs --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --location centralus --sku Standard_ZRS</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0238","card":"q-az-900-036-redundancy","sec":"az-900-s029","q":"Which <code>--sku</code> values create LRS, GRS and GZRS storage accounts?","a":"<p><code>Standard_LRS</code>, <code>Standard_GRS</code> and <code>Standard_GZRS</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>--location centralus --sku Standard_LRS\n--location centralus --sku Standard_GRS\n--location centralus --sku Standard_GZRS</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0239","card":"q-az-900-036-redundancy","sec":"az-900-s029","q":"How do you check the redundancy of an existing Azure storage account with the CLI?","a":"<p>Query <code>sku.name</code> with <code>az storage account show</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az storage account show --name az900lrs --resource-group AZ900 --query &quot;sku.name&quot; -o tsv</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0240","card":"q-az-900-037-storage-account-types","sec":"az-900-s030","q":"What are the four Azure storage account types and what does each support?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Standard general-purpose v2</strong> (recommended): Blob, Files, Queue, Table.</li>\n  <li><strong>Premium Block Blobs</strong>: block and append blobs.</li>\n  <li><strong>Premium File Shares</strong>: Azure Files.</li>\n  <li><strong>Premium Page Blobs</strong>: page blobs (VHDs).</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0241","card":"q-az-900-037-storage-account-types","sec":"az-900-s030","q":"Which redundancy options does each Azure storage account type allow?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Redundancy</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Standard general-purpose v2</td><td>LRS, ZRS, GRS, GZRS</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Premium Block Blobs</td><td>LRS, ZRS</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Premium File Shares</td><td>LRS, ZRS</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Premium Page Blobs</td><td>LRS only</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0242","card":"q-az-900-037-storage-account-types","sec":"az-900-s030","q":"Which Azure storage account type is recommended, and what media does it use compared with premium types?","a":"<p>Standard general-purpose v2 is recommended. It uses HDD. All premium types use SSDs.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0243","card":"q-az-900-037-storage-account-types","sec":"az-900-s030","q":"Which Azure CLI command creates a Standard general-purpose v2 storage account?","a":"<p><code>az storage account create</code> with <code>--kind StorageV2</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az storage account create \\\n  --name az900standard --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --location centralus --sku Standard_LRS --kind StorageV2</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0244","card":"q-az-900-037-storage-account-types","sec":"az-900-s030","q":"Which <code>--kind</code> creates a Premium Block Blobs account and which creates a Premium File Shares account?","a":"<p><code>BlockBlobStorage</code> for Premium Block Blobs and <code>FileStorage</code> for Premium File Shares. Both use <code>--sku Premium_LRS</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>--location centralus --sku Premium_LRS --kind BlockBlobStorage\n--location centralus --sku Premium_LRS --kind FileStorage</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0245","card":"q-az-900-037-storage-account-types","sec":"az-900-s030","q":"How do you list all storage accounts in a resource group with their kind and SKU in a table?","a":"<p>Use <code>az storage account list</code> with a <code>--query</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az storage account list --resource-group AZ900 --query &quot;[].{Name:name, Kind:kind, SKU:sku.name}&quot; -o table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0246","card":"q-az-900-037-storage-account-types","sec":"az-900-s030","q":"In Azure, how do you create a Premium Page Blobs storage account with the CLI?","a":"<p>Use <code>--sku Premium_LRS</code> with <code>--kind StorageV2</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az storage account create \\\n  --name az900prempage --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --location centralus --sku Premium_LRS --kind StorageV2</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0247","card":"q-az-900-038-moving-files","sec":"az-900-s031","q":"What are the three Azure tools for moving files and what is each best for?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Type</th><th>Best for</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>AzCopy</strong></td><td>CLI</td><td>Scripting, automation, bulk copies. Manages SAS, tiers</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Storage Explorer</strong></td><td>Desktop GUI (Windows/macOS/Linux)</td><td>Drag-and-drop, container and tier management, SAS generation</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Azure File Sync</strong></td><td>On-prem agent</td><td>Fast local access to Azure Files data</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0248","card":"q-az-900-038-moving-files","sec":"az-900-s031","q":"What is an Azure Shared Access Signature (SAS) token?","a":"<p>A token that gives others controlled, time-limited access. It has a start time, an expiry and permissions (read, list, write...). It expires automatically.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0249","card":"q-az-900-038-moving-files","sec":"az-900-s031","q":"How do you sign in to AzCopy and upload a single file to blob storage?","a":"<p>Run <code>azcopy login</code>, then <code>azcopy copy</code> with the local file and the blob URL.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>azcopy login\nazcopy copy &#x27;./photo.jpg&#x27; &#x27;https://az900storage.blob.core.windows.net/pictures/photo.jpg&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0250","card":"q-az-900-038-moving-files","sec":"az-900-s031","q":"How do you upload a whole directory to blob storage with AzCopy?","a":"<p>Use <code>azcopy copy</code> with <code>--recursive</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>azcopy copy &#x27;./images/&#x27; &#x27;https://az900storage.blob.core.windows.net/pictures/&#x27; --recursive</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0251","card":"q-az-900-038-moving-files","sec":"az-900-s031","q":"How do you download a blob with AzCopy?","a":"<p>Use <code>azcopy copy</code> with the blob URL as source and a local path as target.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>azcopy copy &#x27;https://az900storage.blob.core.windows.net/pictures/photo.jpg&#x27; &#x27;./downloads/&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0252","card":"q-az-900-038-moving-files","sec":"az-900-s031","q":"How do you copy between two storage accounts with AzCopy?","a":"<p>Use <code>azcopy copy</code> with both URLs and <code>--recursive</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>azcopy copy \\\n  &#x27;https://source.blob.core.windows.net/container/*&#x27; \\\n  &#x27;https://destination.blob.core.windows.net/container/&#x27; \\\n  --recursive</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0253","card":"q-az-900-038-moving-files","sec":"az-900-s031","q":"Which AzCopy command syncs a local directory with a blob container?","a":"<p><code>azcopy sync</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>azcopy sync &#x27;./images/&#x27; &#x27;https://az900storage.blob.core.windows.net/pictures/&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0254","card":"q-az-900-038-moving-files","sec":"az-900-s031","q":"How do you generate a SAS token for a container with the Azure CLI, and what do the flags set?","a":"<p>Use <code>az storage container generate-sas</code>. <code>--permissions rl</code> sets read and list, <code>--expiry</code> sets the expiry time.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az storage container generate-sas \\\n  --account-name az900storage \\\n  --name pictures \\\n  --permissions rl \\\n  --expiry 2025-12-31T23:59:00Z \\\n  --output tsv</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0255","card":"q-az-900-038-moving-files","sec":"az-900-s031","q":"How do you use a SAS token with AzCopy?","a":"<p>Append it to the blob URL after a <code>?</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>azcopy copy \\\n  &#x27;https://az900storage.blob.core.windows.net/pictures/photo.jpg?&lt;sas-token&gt;&#x27; \\\n  &#x27;./downloads/&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0256","card":"q-az-900-038-moving-files","sec":"az-900-s031","q":"How do you set up Azure File Sync on an on-premises server?","a":"<p>Install the Azure File Sync agent on the server, then register it with PowerShell.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Register-AzStorageSyncServer -ResourceGroupName &quot;AZ900&quot; -StorageSyncServiceName &quot;myFileSyncService&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0257","card":"q-az-900-039-migration-options","sec":"az-900-s032","q":"What is Azure Migrate and what does it move?","a":"<p>A service that moves servers, databases and web apps from on-prem or other clouds to Azure. It works in three steps: discovery, assessment, migration.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0258","card":"q-az-900-039-migration-options","sec":"az-900-s032","q":"What happens in the Discovery step of Azure Migrate?","a":"<p>The Azure Migrate Appliance (on a dedicated Windows server) collects metadata and performance data and sends it to Azure. It takes about 1 hour for up to 500 servers.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0259","card":"q-az-900-039-migration-options","sec":"az-900-s032","q":"What happens in the Assessment and Migration steps of Azure Migrate?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Assessment</strong>: group resources. Azure recommends VM sizes and disk types from the performance data.</li>\n  <li><strong>Migration</strong>: automated, with test migrations to catch problems first.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0260","card":"q-az-900-039-migration-options","sec":"az-900-s032","q":"What is Azure Data Box used for?","a":"<p>Moving massive data into Azure Storage, especially with limited connectivity.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0261","card":"q-az-900-039-migration-options","sec":"az-900-s032","q":"Compare Data Box Disk, Data Box and Data Box Heavy.","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Offering</th><th>Capacity</th><th>Encryption</th><th>Storage accounts</th><th>Form</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Data Box Disk</strong></td><td>Up to 5 SSDs × ~7 TB (~35 TB)</td><td>AES 128-bit</td><td>1</td><td>SSDs in tamper-resistant enclosure</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Data Box</strong></td><td>Up to 80 TB</td><td>AES 256-bit</td><td>Up to 10</td><td>Ruggedized appliance</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Data Box Heavy</strong></td><td>Up to 1 PB (~770 TB usable)</td><td>AES 256-bit</td><td>Up to 10</td><td>Freight-shipped, on wheeled cart. Has a local web UI</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0262","card":"q-az-900-039-migration-options","sec":"az-900-s032","q":"What is the process for moving data with Azure Data Box?","a":"<p>Order in the portal, Microsoft ships the device, you connect and copy data, ship it back, the data is imported, and the disks are wiped to NIST 800-88 R1. Devices are tamper-resistant, with AES encryption.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0263","card":"q-az-900-039-migration-options","sec":"az-900-s032","q":"Which Azure CLI command checks the status of a Data Box order?","a":"<p><code>az databox job show</code> with a <code>--query \"status\"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az databox job show --resource-group AZ900 --name myDataBoxOrder --query &quot;status&quot; -o tsv</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0264","card":"q-az-900-039-migration-options","sec":"az-900-s032","q":"Which Azure tool fits each data move: servers, databases and web apps; files by script; files by GUI; about 35 TB; up to 80 TB; hundreds of TB?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Scenario</th><th>Tool</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Servers, databases, web apps</td><td>Azure Migrate</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Files via script/CLI</td><td>AzCopy</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Files via GUI</td><td>Storage Explorer</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>~35 TB, limited connectivity</td><td>Data Box Disk</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Up to 80 TB</td><td>Data Box</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Hundreds of TB, up to 1 PB</td><td>Data Box Heavy</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0265","card":"q-az-900-039-migration-options","sec":"az-900-s032","q":"In Azure, how do you create an Azure Data Box order with the CLI?","a":"<p>Use <code>az databox job create</code> with the resource group, a name, a location and <code>--sku DataBox</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az databox job create \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --name myDataBoxOrder \\\n  --location centralus \\\n  --sku DataBox \\</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0266","card":"q-az-900-040-directory-services","sec":"az-900-s033","q":"What is the difference between authentication and authorization?","a":"<p>Authentication is who or what is accessing. Authorization is what that identity can do.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0267","card":"q-az-900-040-directory-services","sec":"az-900-s033","q":"What is Azure AD (Entra ID)?","a":"<p>A cloud identity service that authenticates and authorizes access to Azure, third-party and on-prem resources. It comes with your Azure subscription.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0268","card":"q-az-900-040-directory-services","sec":"az-900-s033","q":"What are the three Azure AD identity types?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Users</strong>: people in your org or invited external users.</li>\n  <li><strong>Service principals</strong> (enterprise applications): apps registered in Azure AD, so users sign in to external services with their Azure AD account. Revoking the user revokes access to all linked apps at once (for example AWS as an enterprise app).</li>\n  <li><strong>Managed identities</strong>: let Azure resources authenticate to other Azure services without stored credentials.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0269","card":"q-az-900-040-directory-services","sec":"az-900-s033","q":"Which Azure CLI command lists Azure AD users with their name and UPN?","a":"<p><code>az ad user list</code> with a <code>--query</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az ad user list --query &quot;[].{Name:displayName, UPN:userPrincipalName}&quot; -o table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0270","card":"q-az-900-040-directory-services","sec":"az-900-s033","q":"How do you create a service principal for an application with the Azure CLI?","a":"<p>Run <code>az ad sp create-for-rbac</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az ad sp create-for-rbac --name &quot;myApp&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0271","card":"q-az-900-040-directory-services","sec":"az-900-s033","q":"How do you list enterprise applications and delete a service principal with the Azure CLI?","a":"<p>Use <code>az ad sp list</code> and <code>az ad sp delete</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az ad sp list --all --query &quot;[].{Name:displayName, AppId:appId}&quot; -o table\naz ad sp delete --id &lt;app-id&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0272","card":"q-az-900-040-directory-services","sec":"az-900-s033","q":"How do you enable a system-assigned managed identity on a VM and on a web app?","a":"<p>Use <code>az vm identity assign</code> and <code>az webapp identity assign</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az vm identity assign --resource-group AZ900 --name VM1\naz webapp identity assign --resource-group AZ900 --name az900wa</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0273","card":"q-az-900-040-directory-services","sec":"az-900-s033","q":"Azure AD vs Azure AD Domain Services: what type is each and which protocols do they use?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th></th><th>Azure AD</th><th>Azure AD Domain Services</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Type</td><td>Cloud-native identity</td><td>Managed Windows AD Domain Services in the cloud</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Protocols</td><td>OAuth, SAML, OpenID Connect</td><td>LDAP, Kerberos, NTLM</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0274","card":"q-az-900-040-directory-services","sec":"az-900-s033","q":"When do you use Azure AD and when do you use Azure AD Domain Services?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Azure AD</strong>: cloud apps, third-party apps, Azure resources.</li>\n  <li><strong>Azure AD Domain Services</strong>: legacy apps that lack modern auth, integration with on-prem AD, lift-and-shift.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0275","card":"q-az-900-040-directory-services","sec":"az-900-s033","q":"What components make up Azure AD and Azure AD Domain Services?","a":"<p>Azure AD has users, groups, service principals and managed identities. Azure AD Domain Services has managed domains and replica sets.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0276","card":"q-az-900-040-directory-services","sec":"az-900-s033","q":"In Azure, which command shows the managed identity of a VM?","a":"<p><code>az vm identity show</code> shows it.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az vm identity show --resource-group AZ900 --name VM1</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0277","card":"q-az-900-040-directory-services","sec":"az-900-s033","q":"How do you invite an external user in Azure AD with the Azure CLI (Kelly Green example)?","a":"<p>Use <code>az ad user create</code> with a display name, a user principal name and a password.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az ad user create \\\n  --display-name &quot;Kelly Green&quot; \\\n  --user-principal-name kelly@&lt;tenant-domain&gt;.onmicrosoft.com \\\n  --password &quot;&lt;secure-password&gt;&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0278","card":"q-az-900-041-authentication-methods","sec":"az-900-s034","q":"What is single sign-on (SSO) and what extends it to on-prem?","a":"<p>SSO means you authenticate once and reuse that sign-in for all resources. <strong>Azure AD Connect</strong> extends SSO to on-prem.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0279","card":"q-az-900-041-authentication-methods","sec":"az-900-s034","q":"What are the two Azure AD Connect SSO methods and how do they differ?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Password Hash Synchronization</strong>: the password is hashed, the hash is stored in Azure AD, and logins compare hashes.</li>\n  <li><strong>Pass-Through Authentication</strong>: credentials go to an on-prem agent and are validated against on-prem AD, and the result goes back to Azure AD via AD Connect.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0280","card":"q-az-900-041-authentication-methods","sec":"az-900-s034","q":"What are the three factor types in multi-factor authentication, and how many does Azure MFA use?","a":"<p>Something you <strong>know</strong> (password, PIN), <strong>have</strong> (phone, security key) and <strong>are</strong> (fingerprint, face, retina). Two-factor is two of them, three-factor is all three. Azure MFA uses two-factor.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0281","card":"q-az-900-041-authentication-methods","sec":"az-900-s034","q":"What are the requirements and limits for Azure MFA?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>It needs Azure AD Premium (not the free tier).</li>\n  <li>It is enabled per user.</li>\n  <li>Guest users need a conditional access policy for MFA.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0282","card":"q-az-900-041-authentication-methods","sec":"az-900-s034","q":"Which Azure portal path enables per-user MFA?","a":"<p>Azure AD → Users → All Users → Per-user MFA → Select user → Enable.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0283","card":"q-az-900-041-authentication-methods","sec":"az-900-s034","q":"What does passwordless authentication replace, and what are the passwordless methods?","a":"<p>It replaces \"something you know\". Methods:</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>How</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>FIDO2 security key</td><td>Cryptographic keys on a phone or USB key</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Microsoft Authenticator app</td><td>Push notification, enter the shown number, confirm with biometrics/PIN</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Text message (SMS)</td><td>Code sent by text, entered on the computer</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Temporary Access Pass (TAP)</td><td>Time-limited string for initial setup or a lost device</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Certificate-based</td><td>Digital certificate</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Windows Hello for Business</td><td>Face biometrics on Windows devices</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0284","card":"q-az-900-041-authentication-methods","sec":"az-900-s034","q":"What is a Temporary Access Pass (TAP) used for?","a":"<p>A time-limited string for initial setup or a lost device.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0285","card":"q-az-900-041-authentication-methods","sec":"az-900-s034","q":"How do you create a Temporary Access Pass for a user through Microsoft Graph with <code>az rest</code>?","a":"<p>POST to the user's <code>temporaryAccessPassMethods</code> endpoint with a lifetime and a single-use flag.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az rest --method POST \\\n  --uri &quot;https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/users/&lt;user-id&gt;/authentication/temporaryAccessPassMethods&quot; \\\n  --headers &quot;Content-Type=application/json&quot; \\\n  --body &#x27;{&quot;lifetimeInMinutes&quot;: 60, &quot;isUsableOnce&quot;: true}&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0286","card":"q-az-900-041-authentication-methods","sec":"az-900-s034","q":"In Azure AD, how do you enable the FIDO2 security key method for the tenant with the CLI?","a":"<p>Send a PATCH to the <code>fido2</code> authentication method configuration in the Microsoft Graph API and set the state to enabled.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az rest --method PATCH \\\n  --uri &quot;https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/policies/authenticationMethodsPolicy/authenticationMethodConfigurations/fido2&quot; \\\n  --headers &quot;Content-Type=application/json&quot; \\\n  --body &#x27;{&quot;state&quot;: &quot;enabled&quot;}&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0287","card":"q-az-900-041-authentication-methods","sec":"az-900-s034","q":"In Azure AD, how do you check a user's authentication methods (for example, whether MFA is enabled) with the CLI?","a":"<p>Send a GET to the user's <code>authentication/methods</code> endpoint in the Microsoft Graph API.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az rest --method GET \\\n  --uri &quot;https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/users/&lt;user-id&gt;/authentication/methods&quot; \\\n  --headers &quot;Content-Type=application/json&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0288","card":"q-az-900-041-authentication-methods","sec":"az-900-s034","q":"After installing Azure AD Connect on the on-premises server, which PowerShell command configures SSO?","a":"<p><code>Set-MsolDomainAuthentication</code> with the tenant domain and <code>Managed</code> authentication.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Set-MsolDomainAuthentication \\\n  -DomainName &quot;&lt;tenant-domain&gt;.onmicrosoft.com&quot; \\\n  -Authentication Managed</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0289","card":"q-az-900-042-conditional-access","sec":"az-900-s035","q":"What is Azure Conditional Access and when is it important?","a":"<p>Policies that turn signals into decisions. It is important for BYOD.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0290","card":"q-az-900-042-conditional-access","sec":"az-900-s035","q":"What signals and decisions does Conditional Access use?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Signals (inputs)</strong>: user identity, location, device and OS, application, real-time risk (Azure AD Identity Protection, Defender for Cloud Apps).</li>\n  <li><strong>Decisions</strong>: block access, allow with MFA, require compliant device, require approved client app.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0291","card":"q-az-900-042-conditional-access","sec":"az-900-s035","q":"How do you list all Conditional Access policies with <code>az rest</code>?","a":"<p>Send a GET to the Microsoft Graph <code>conditionalAccess/policies</code> endpoint.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az rest --method GET \\\n  --uri &quot;https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/identity/conditionalAccess/policies&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0292","card":"q-az-900-042-conditional-access","sec":"az-900-s035","q":"What does the <code>grantControls</code> block do in a Conditional Access policy that requires MFA for all users?","a":"<p>It sets the decision. In a policy that requires MFA for all users, <code>\"builtInControls\": [\"mfa\"]</code> requires MFA, and the conditions include all users and all applications.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&quot;grantControls&quot;: {\n  &quot;operator&quot;: &quot;OR&quot;,\n  &quot;builtInControls&quot;: [&quot;mfa&quot;]\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0293","card":"q-az-900-042-conditional-access","sec":"az-900-s035","q":"In Azure AD, how do you create a Conditional Access policy that requires MFA for all users with the CLI?","a":"<p>Send a POST to the <code>conditionalAccess/policies</code> endpoint in the Microsoft Graph API with the policy body.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az rest --method POST \\\n  --uri &quot;https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/identity/conditionalAccess/policies&quot; \\\n  --headers &quot;Content-Type=application/json&quot; \\\n  --body &#x27;{\n    &quot;displayName&quot;: &quot;Require MFA for all users&quot;,\n    &quot;state&quot;: &quot;enabled&quot;,\n    &quot;conditions&quot;: {\n      &quot;users&quot;: { &quot;includeUsers&quot;: [&quot;All&quot;] },\n      &quot;applications&quot;: { &quot;includeApplications&quot;: [&quot;All&quot;] }\n    },</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0294","card":"q-az-900-043-rbac","sec":"az-900-s036","q":"What does Azure RBAC control, and what are its three elements?","a":"<p>What an authenticated identity can do.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Security principal</strong></td><td>Who: user, group, service principal, managed identity</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Role definition</strong></td><td>What: permissions grouped in a role (built-in or custom)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Scope</strong></td><td>Where: management group, subscription, resource group or resource</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0295","card":"q-az-900-043-rbac","sec":"az-900-s036","q":"Are Azure RBAC rules additive or restrictive, and what does that mean for scopes?","a":"<p>They are additive. A broader role at a higher scope overrides a more restrictive role at a lower scope.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0296","card":"q-az-900-043-rbac","sec":"az-900-s036","q":"What do the Azure built-in roles Owner, Contributor, Reader and Website Contributor allow?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Built-in role</th><th>Permissions</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Owner</strong></td><td>Full access and can assign roles</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Contributor</strong></td><td>Full access, cannot assign roles</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Reader</strong></td><td>View only</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Website Contributor</strong></td><td>Manage web apps</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0297","card":"q-az-900-043-rbac","sec":"az-900-s036","q":"How do you list all built-in roles and the roles for web apps with the Azure CLI?","a":"<p>Use <code>az role definition list</code>, with a <code>contains</code> filter for web apps.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az role definition list --query &quot;[].{Name:roleName, Description:description}&quot; -o table\naz role definition list --query &quot;[?contains(roleName, &#x27;Website&#x27;)]&quot; -o table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0298","card":"q-az-900-043-rbac","sec":"az-900-s036","q":"How do you assign the Website Contributor role to a user on a web app?","a":"<p>Use <code>az role assignment create</code> with <code>--assignee</code>, <code>--role</code> and <code>--scope</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az role assignment create \\\n  --assignee &quot;kelly@&lt;tenant-domain&gt;.onmicrosoft.com&quot; \\\n  --role &quot;Website Contributor&quot; \\\n  --scope &quot;/subscriptions/&lt;sub-id&gt;/resourceGroups/AZ900/providers/Microsoft.Web/sites/az900wa&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0299","card":"q-az-900-043-rbac","sec":"az-900-s036","q":"How do you list and remove Azure role assignments for a resource?","a":"<p>Use <code>az role assignment list</code> and <code>az role assignment delete</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az role assignment list \\\n  --scope &quot;/subscriptions/&lt;sub-id&gt;/resourceGroups/AZ900/providers/Microsoft.Web/sites/az900wa&quot; \\\n  --output table\naz role assignment delete \\\n  --assignee &quot;kelly@&lt;tenant-domain&gt;.onmicrosoft.com&quot; \\\n  --role &quot;Website Contributor&quot; \\\n  --scope &quot;/subscriptions/&lt;sub-id&gt;/resourceGroups/AZ900/providers/Microsoft.Web/sites/az900wa&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0300","card":"q-az-900-043-rbac","sec":"az-900-s036","q":"Which Azure CLI command creates a custom role, and what fields does the JSON definition use?","a":"<p><code>az role definition create --role-definition</code>. The JSON has Name, Description, Actions, NotActions and AssignableScopes.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az role definition create --role-definition &#x27;{\n  &quot;Name&quot;: &quot;Custom App Reader&quot;,\n  &quot;Description&quot;: &quot;Can view web apps but not modify them&quot;,\n  &quot;Actions&quot;: [\n    &quot;Microsoft.Web/sites/read&quot;\n  ],\n  &quot;NotActions&quot;: [],\n  &quot;AssignableScopes&quot;: [\n    &quot;/subscriptions/&lt;sub-id&gt;/resourceGroups/AZ900&quot;\n  ]\n}&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0301","card":"q-az-900-043-rbac","sec":"az-900-s036","q":"How do you assign a custom role to a user on a resource group?","a":"<p>Use <code>az role assignment create</code> with <code>--role</code> and <code>--resource-group</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az role assignment create \\\n  --assignee &quot;jim@&lt;tenant-domain&gt;.onmicrosoft.com&quot; \\\n  --role &quot;Custom App Reader&quot; \\\n  --resource-group AZ900</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0302","card":"q-az-900-044-zero-trust-and-defense-in-depth","sec":"az-900-s037","q":"What is Zero Trust in Azure?","a":"<p>A model that assumes every access is a breach. It covers endpoints, data, apps, infrastructure and network. Apps must be designed for the lowest access necessary.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0303","card":"q-az-900-044-zero-trust-and-defense-in-depth","sec":"az-900-s037","q":"What are the Zero Trust principles and how is each implemented?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Principle</th><th>Implementation</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Verify explicitly</td><td>MFA for every user</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Least-privilege access</td><td>Grant the minimum needed</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Assume breach</td><td>Conditional Access to secure the environment</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0304","card":"q-az-900-044-zero-trust-and-defense-in-depth","sec":"az-900-s037","q":"What is defense in depth?","a":"<p>Layered protection, so a breach of one layer is still caught by others (castle doctrine).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0305","card":"q-az-900-044-zero-trust-and-defense-in-depth","sec":"az-900-s037","q":"What are the defense in depth layers from outer to inner, with their Azure equivalents?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Azure equivalent</th><th>Castle</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Physical</td><td>Data center security</td><td>Stone walls</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Identity and access</td><td>Azure AD, MFA, Conditional Access</td><td>Gate with guards</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Perimeter</td><td>DDoS protection, firewalls</td><td>Moat</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Network</td><td>NSGs, VNet segmentation, private endpoints</td><td>High walls</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Compute</td><td>VM security, patching, endpoint protection</td><td>Archers</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Application</td><td>Secure coding, vulnerability scanning</td><td>Inner defenses</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Data</td><td>Encryption at rest and in transit, access controls</td><td>Soldiers guarding the vault</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0306","card":"q-az-900-045-microsoft-defender-for-cloud","sec":"az-900-s038","q":"What does Microsoft Defender for Cloud protect?","a":"<p>Resources across Azure, on-premises and other clouds.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0307","card":"q-az-900-045-microsoft-defender-for-cloud","sec":"az-900-s038","q":"What are the capabilities of Microsoft Defender for Cloud?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Security posture management: continuously assesses and finds vulnerabilities.</li>\n  <li>Regulatory compliance (HIPAA, GDPR...).</li>\n  <li>Workload protection for VMs, servers, apps and data.</li>\n  <li>Real-time threat detection and alerts.</li>\n  <li>Proactive best-practice guidance.</li>\n  <li>Automatically scans newly deployed resources.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0308","card":"q-az-900-045-microsoft-defender-for-cloud","sec":"az-900-s038","q":"How do you enable Microsoft Defender for Cloud plans for VMs, App Services and storage accounts with the Azure CLI?","a":"<p>Use <code>az security pricing create</code> with <code>--tier Standard</code> for each plan.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az security pricing create --name VirtualMachines --tier Standard\naz security pricing create --name AppServices --tier Standard\naz security pricing create --name StorageAccounts --tier Standard</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0309","card":"q-az-900-045-microsoft-defender-for-cloud","sec":"az-900-s038","q":"Which Azure CLI commands show the secure score, recommendations, alerts and regulatory compliance in Defender for Cloud?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az security secure-score list --output table\naz security assessment list --output table\naz security alert list --output table\naz security regulatory-compliance-standards list --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0310","card":"q-az-900-046-what-affects-cost","sec":"az-900-s039","q":"What are the three main factors that affect Azure cost?","a":"<p>Meters, purchasing options and region.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0311","card":"q-az-900-046-what-affects-cost","sec":"az-900-s039","q":"How do meters affect Azure cost?","a":"<p>Many resources bill per metered usage. Blob Storage bills operations plus per-GB transfer. VNet peering bills per GB, and same-region peering is much cheaper than cross-region.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0312","card":"q-az-900-046-what-affects-cost","sec":"az-900-s039","q":"What are Azure Reservations, Spot VMs and Hybrid Use Benefit, and how much do they save?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Savings</th><th>What</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Azure Reservations</strong></td><td>Up to 72%</td><td>1- or 3-year commitment (VMs, databases...)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Azure Spot VMs</strong></td><td>Up to 90%</td><td>Unused capacity, for short/interruptible workloads</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Hybrid Use Benefit</strong></td><td>Significant</td><td>Bring your own Windows or SQL Server license</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0313","card":"q-az-900-046-what-affects-cost","sec":"az-900-s039","q":"Why do Azure prices differ by region?","a":"<p>Power, network and facilities costs differ, even within a country. Check the pricing page before choosing a region.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0314","card":"q-az-900-046-what-affects-cost","sec":"az-900-s039","q":"How do you view meter details for a resource with the Azure CLI?","a":"<p>Use <code>az consumption usage list</code> with a date range and a <code>--query</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az consumption usage list \\\n  --start-date 2025-01-01 --end-date 2025-01-31 \\\n  --query &quot;[].{Resource:instanceName, Meter:meterName, Quantity:quantity, Cost:pretaxCost}&quot; \\\n  --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0315","card":"q-az-900-046-what-affects-cost","sec":"az-900-s039","q":"Which flags create an Azure Spot VM with the CLI?","a":"<p><code>--priority Spot</code>, <code>--eviction-policy Deallocate</code> and <code>--max-price</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az vm create \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --name mySpotVM \\\n  --image Ubuntu2204 \\\n  --priority Spot \\\n  --eviction-policy Deallocate \\\n  --max-price 0.05 \\\n  --admin-username azureuser \\\n  --generate-ssh-keys</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0316","card":"q-az-900-046-what-affects-cost","sec":"az-900-s039","q":"How do you list available VM reservations with the Azure CLI?","a":"<p>Use <code>az reservations catalog show</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az reservations catalog show \\\n  --reserved-resource-type VirtualMachines \\\n  --location centralus \\\n  --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0317","card":"q-az-900-046-what-affects-cost","sec":"az-900-s039","q":"Which flag applies Hybrid Use Benefit when creating a Windows VM?","a":"<p><code>--license-type Windows_Server</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az vm create \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --name myHybridVM \\\n  --image Win2022Datacenter \\\n  --license-type Windows_Server \\\n  --admin-username azureuser \\\n  --admin-password &quot;&lt;secure-password&gt;&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0318","card":"q-az-900-046-what-affects-cost","sec":"az-900-s039","q":"In Azure, how do you compare VM pricing across regions with the CLI, and which tool gives detailed cost comparisons?","a":"<p>Run <code>az vm list-skus</code> once per region, filtering on the size name. Use the Azure Pricing Calculator for detailed cost comparisons.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az vm list-skus \\\n  --location centralus \\\n  --resource-type virtualMachines \\\n  --query &quot;[?name==&#x27;Standard_D2s_v3&#x27;].{Name:name, Location:locationInfo[0].location}&quot; \\\n  --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0319","card":"q-az-900-047-pricing-calculator-vs-tco-calculator","sec":"az-900-s040","q":"Azure Pricing Calculator vs TCO Calculator: what is the purpose, input, output and use of each?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th></th><th>Pricing Calculator</th><th>TCO Calculator</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Purpose</td><td>Estimate cost of <strong>Azure resources</strong> before deploying</td><td>Forecast <strong>savings migrating from on-prem to Azure</strong></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Input</td><td>Azure resource configuration</td><td>On-prem workload details and assumptions</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Output</td><td>Estimated monthly Azure cost (estimate, not a quote). Save, export, share</td><td>Savings comparison on-prem vs Azure, can download or share</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Use for</td><td>Planning new deployments</td><td>Justifying a migration</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0320","card":"q-az-900-047-pricing-calculator-vs-tco-calculator","sec":"az-900-s040","q":"What changes the price in the Azure Pricing Calculator?","a":"<p>Region, instance size, App Service tier (Basic &lt; Standard &lt; Premium), storage redundancy (LRS &lt; ZRS &lt; GRS &lt; GZRS), Hybrid Use Benefit, and operations count.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0321","card":"q-az-900-047-pricing-calculator-vs-tco-calculator","sec":"az-900-s040","q":"What are the three steps of the Azure TCO Calculator?","a":"<ol>\n  <li><strong>Define workloads</strong> (servers, web apps, databases, storage).</li>\n  <li><strong>Adjust assumptions</strong> (software assurance, geo-redundancy, electricity, storage, IT labor, hardware costs).</li>\n  <li><strong>View report</strong> (savings breakdown across compute, data center, networking, storage).</li>\n</ol>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0322","card":"q-az-900-048-cost-management-and-billing-tool","sec":"az-900-s041","q":"What is the Azure Cost Management and Billing tool for?","a":"<p>Analyzing costs in the portal after deployment.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0323","card":"q-az-900-048-cost-management-and-billing-tool","sec":"az-900-s041","q":"What features does Azure Cost Management and Billing include?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Cost analysis</strong>: accumulated costs, forecast, breakdown by service/region.</li>\n  <li><strong>Budgets</strong>: name, period and threshold.</li>\n  <li><strong>Cost alerts</strong>: notify when spending nears or passes a budget (including anomaly alerts).</li>\n  <li><strong>Invoices and payments</strong>.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0324","card":"q-az-900-048-cost-management-and-billing-tool","sec":"az-900-s041","q":"How do you create a monthly budget of 500 with the Azure CLI?","a":"<p>Use <code>az consumption budget create</code> with <code>--amount</code>, <code>--category Cost</code> and <code>--time-grain Monthly</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az consumption budget create \\\n  --budget-name MonthlyBudget \\\n  --amount 500 \\\n  --category Cost \\\n  --time-grain Monthly \\\n  --start-date 2025-01-01 \\\n  --end-date 2025-12-31</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0325","card":"q-az-900-048-cost-management-and-billing-tool","sec":"az-900-s041","q":"How do you list existing budgets with the Azure CLI, and where do you see the cost forecast?","a":"<p>Run <code>az consumption budget list</code>. The forecast is in the Azure Portal under Cost Management → Cost Analysis → Forecast view.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az consumption budget list --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0326","card":"q-az-900-049-tags","sec":"az-900-s042","q":"What are Azure tags and what are they used for?","a":"<p>Name-value pairs on any resource. They filter portal views and categorize spending on invoices. They auto-complete from existing tags, and a resource can have several.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0327","card":"q-az-900-049-tags","sec":"az-900-s042","q":"What are example Azure tags?","a":"<p><code>department=marketing</code>, <code>usage=AZ900 live training</code> and <code>company=JimCo</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0328","card":"q-az-900-049-tags","sec":"az-900-s042","q":"How do you add tags to a VM with the Azure CLI?","a":"<p>Use <code>az resource tag</code> with <code>--tags</code> and the resource type.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az resource tag \\\n  --tags department=marketing usage=&quot;AZ900 live training&quot; \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 --name VM1 \\\n  --resource-type Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0329","card":"q-az-900-049-tags","sec":"az-900-s042","q":"How do you tag a whole resource group with the Azure CLI?","a":"<p>Use <code>az group update</code> with <code>--tags</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az group update --name AZ900 --tags company=JimCo</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0330","card":"q-az-900-049-tags","sec":"az-900-s042","q":"How do you list resources with a given tag, and all tags in a subscription?","a":"<p>Use <code>az resource list --tag</code> and <code>az tag list</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az resource list --tag department=marketing --output table\naz tag list --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0331","card":"q-az-900-049-tags","sec":"az-900-s042","q":"In Azure, how do you remove a tag from a resource with the CLI?","a":"<p>Run <code>az resource tag</code> again with the tag set that leaves out the tag you want to remove.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az resource tag \\\n  --tags department=marketing \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 --name VM1 \\\n  --resource-type Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0332","card":"q-az-900-050-10-governance-and-compliance","sec":"az-900-s043","q":"What are the three Azure governance tools, their purpose and scope?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Scope</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Blueprints</strong></td><td>Reusable package of resource groups, ARM templates, policy assignments and RBAC assignments</td><td>Subscription / management group</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Policy</strong></td><td>Enforce rules on resource creation and management</td><td>Subscription / resource group / resource</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Resource locks</strong></td><td>Prevent change or deletion</td><td>Any resource</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0333","card":"q-az-900-051-azure-blueprints","sec":"az-900-s044","q":"What are Azure Blueprints used for?","a":"<p>Reusing configuration, policy and governance for complex deployments.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0334","card":"q-az-900-051-azure-blueprints","sec":"az-900-s044","q":"What is the Azure Blueprints workflow?","a":"<p><strong>Create</strong> (define artifacts), <strong>Publish</strong> (save to a subscription or management group so it can be assigned), then <strong>Assign</strong> (resources are created automatically).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0335","card":"q-az-900-051-azure-blueprints","sec":"az-900-s044","q":"Why must you name a target subscription when assigning an Azure Blueprint to a management group?","a":"<p>Management groups only hold subscriptions or other management groups.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0336","card":"q-az-900-052-azure-policy","sec":"az-900-s045","q":"What is Azure Policy?","a":"<p>It defines rules applied when resources are created and managed. Examples: VMs must be a certain size, resources must be in a certain region, certain resource types must deploy together.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0337","card":"q-az-900-052-azure-policy","sec":"az-900-s045","q":"What are the Azure Policy effects?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Effect</th><th>Behavior</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Append</strong></td><td>Adds properties to a resource (for example auto-add a tag)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Audit</strong></td><td>Logs a warning on non-compliance</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>AuditIfNotExists</strong></td><td>Logs a warning if a required related resource is missing</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>DeployIfNotExists</strong></td><td>Deploys the required related resource if missing</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Deny</strong></td><td>Blocks the create or update</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Disabled</strong></td><td>Policy is off</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0338","card":"q-az-900-052-azure-policy","sec":"az-900-s045","q":"What is the difference between the Audit and Deny effects in Azure Policy?","a":"<p>Audit logs a warning on non-compliance. Deny blocks the create or update.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0339","card":"q-az-900-052-azure-policy","sec":"az-900-s045","q":"What is the difference between AuditIfNotExists and DeployIfNotExists?","a":"<p>AuditIfNotExists logs a warning if a required related resource is missing. DeployIfNotExists deploys that required related resource.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0340","card":"q-az-900-052-azure-policy","sec":"az-900-s045","q":"How do you list all built-in Azure policy definitions with the CLI?","a":"<p>Use <code>az policy definition list</code> and filter on <code>policyType=='BuiltIn'</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az policy definition list --query &quot;[?policyType==&#x27;BuiltIn&#x27;].{Name:displayName}&quot; --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0341","card":"q-az-900-052-azure-policy","sec":"az-900-s045","q":"How do you assign the \"Allowed locations\" policy to restrict resources to specific regions?","a":"<p>Use <code>az policy assignment create</code> with <code>--params</code> listing the allowed locations.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az policy assignment create \\\n  --name &quot;AllowedLocations&quot; \\\n  --policy &quot;/providers/Microsoft.Authorization/policyDefinitions/e56962a6-4747-49cd-b67b-bf8b01975c4c&quot; \\\n  --params &#x27;{&quot;listOfAllowedLocations&quot;: {&quot;value&quot;: [&quot;centralus&quot;, &quot;eastus&quot;]}}&#x27; \\\n  --scope &quot;/subscriptions/&lt;sub-id&gt;&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0342","card":"q-az-900-052-azure-policy","sec":"az-900-s045","q":"How do you assign a policy that requires a tag on resources in a resource group?","a":"<p>Use <code>az policy assignment create</code> with a <code>tagName</code> parameter and the resource group as scope.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az policy assignment create \\\n  --name &quot;RequireDeptTag&quot; \\\n  --policy &quot;/providers/Microsoft.Authorization/policyDefinitions/871b6d14-10aa-478d-b466-ef6698305b4c&quot; \\\n  --params &#x27;{&quot;tagName&quot;: {&quot;value&quot;: &quot;department&quot;}}&#x27; \\\n  --scope &quot;/subscriptions/&lt;sub-id&gt;/resourceGroups/AZ900&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0343","card":"q-az-900-052-azure-policy","sec":"az-900-s045","q":"How do you check Azure Policy compliance and list non-compliant resources?","a":"<p>Use <code>az policy state summarize</code> and <code>az policy state list</code> with a filter.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az policy state summarize --output table\naz policy state list \\\n  --filter &quot;complianceState eq &#x27;NonCompliant&#x27;&quot; \\\n  --query &quot;[].{Resource:resourceId, Policy:policyAssignmentName}&quot; \\\n  --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0344","card":"q-az-900-052-azure-policy","sec":"az-900-s045","q":"How is a custom policy definition structured that denies VMs larger than Standard_D4s_v3?","a":"<p>A rule with an <code>if</code> condition and a <code>then</code> effect of <code>deny</code>, created with <code>az policy definition create</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az policy definition create \\\n  --name &quot;RestrictVMSize&quot; \\\n  --display-name &quot;Restrict VM sizes&quot; \\\n  --rules &#x27;{\n    &quot;if&quot;: {\n      &quot;allOf&quot;: [\n        {&quot;field&quot;: &quot;type&quot;, &quot;equals&quot;: &quot;Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines&quot;},\n        {&quot;not&quot;: {&quot;field&quot;: &quot;Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/sku.name&quot;, &quot;in&quot;: [&quot;Standard_D2s_v3&quot;, &quot;Standard_D4s_v3&quot;]}}\n      ]\n    },\n    &quot;then&quot;: {&quot;effect&quot;: &quot;deny&quot;}\n  }&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0345","card":"q-az-900-053-resource-locks","sec":"az-900-s046","q":"What are Azure resource locks and how do they differ from RBAC?","a":"<p>They prevent changes or deletion and apply to all users, unlike RBAC. They are available on every resource (Settings → Locks). A user with a restricted role (for example Website Contributor) cannot remove locks.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0346","card":"q-az-900-053-resource-locks","sec":"az-900-s046","q":"What is the difference between a Read-Only lock and a Delete lock in Azure?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Lock</th><th>Modify?</th><th>Delete?</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Read-Only</strong></td><td>No</td><td>No</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Delete</strong> (CanNotDelete)</td><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0347","card":"q-az-900-053-resource-locks","sec":"az-900-s046","q":"How do you create a delete lock on a web app with the Azure CLI?","a":"<p>Use <code>az lock create</code> with <code>--lock-type CanNotDelete</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az lock create \\\n  --name &quot;InternProtect&quot; \\\n  --lock-type CanNotDelete \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --resource-name az900wa \\\n  --resource-type Microsoft.Web/sites</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0348","card":"q-az-900-053-resource-locks","sec":"az-900-s046","q":"How do you create a read-only lock on a storage account with the Azure CLI?","a":"<p>Use <code>az lock create</code> with <code>--lock-type ReadOnly</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az lock create \\\n  --name &quot;StorageReadOnly&quot; \\\n  --lock-type ReadOnly \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --resource-name az900storage \\\n  --resource-type Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0349","card":"q-az-900-053-resource-locks","sec":"az-900-s046","q":"How do you list locks in a resource group and delete a lock?","a":"<p>Use <code>az lock list</code> and <code>az lock delete</code>. Deleting needs sufficient permissions.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az lock list --resource-group AZ900 --output table\naz lock delete \\\n  --name &quot;InternProtect&quot; \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --resource-name az900wa \\\n  --resource-type Microsoft.Web/sites</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0350","card":"q-az-900-054-infrastructure-as-code-iac","sec":"az-900-s047","q":"What is Infrastructure as Code (IaC) in Azure?","a":"<p>A DevOps approach with a descriptive (declarative) model to define and deploy networks, VMs, load balancers and so on. The same IaC model gives the same environment every time.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0351","card":"q-az-900-054-infrastructure-as-code-iac","sec":"az-900-s047","q":"What are the Azure options for IaC?","a":"<p>ARM templates (JSON) and Bicep.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0352","card":"q-az-900-054-infrastructure-as-code-iac","sec":"az-900-s047","q":"How do you deploy an ARM template or a Bicep file to a resource group?","a":"<p>Use <code>az deployment group create</code> with <code>--template-file</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az deployment group create \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --template-file azuredeploy.json\naz deployment group create \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --template-file main.bicep</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0353","card":"q-az-900-054-infrastructure-as-code-iac","sec":"az-900-s047","q":"What does a Bicep file that deploys a Standard_LRS storage account look like?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>resource storageAccount &#x27;Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts@2023-01-01&#x27; = {\n  name: &#x27;iacdemostorage&#x27;\n  location: resourceGroup().location\n  sku: { name: &#x27;Standard_LRS&#x27; }\n  kind: &#x27;StorageV2&#x27;\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0354","card":"q-az-900-055-azure-portal","sec":"az-900-s048","q":"What is the Azure Portal and what can you customize?","a":"<p>A web GUI that is fully customizable. It has favorites pinned in the left menu, a search bar, All Services, a docked or flyout menu, themes (including high contrast), and a Home or Dashboard startup view.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0355","card":"q-az-900-055-azure-portal","sec":"az-900-s048","q":"What are Azure Portal dashboards?","a":"<p>Custom views with real-time data from Azure Monitor and other services. You can keep several, with tiles you can add, resize and reposition (Edit → drag tiles → Save). They are saved to your subscription and follow you to any device.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0356","card":"q-az-900-055-azure-portal","sec":"az-900-s048","q":"How can you create an Azure dashboard programmatically?","a":"<p>Dashboards are portal-only, but you can create them with ARM templates. Export a dashboard from the portal (Dashboard → Share → Download) or deploy a template of type <code>Microsoft.Portal/dashboards</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az deployment group create \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --template-file dashboard.json</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0357","card":"q-az-900-055-azure-portal","sec":"az-900-s048","q":"Which CLI commands match the portal's \"All Resources\" view and common resource lists?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az resource list --output table\naz vm list --output table\naz webapp list --output table\naz storage account list --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0358","card":"q-az-900-056-command-line-tools","sec":"az-900-s049","q":"Azure PowerShell vs Azure CLI: how do they differ in style, packaging, default output and best use?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th></th><th>Azure PowerShell</th><th>Azure CLI</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Style</td><td>Cmdlets: <code>Get-AzResource</code></td><td>Commands: <code>az resource list</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Packaging</td><td>Az module</td><td>CLI binary</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Default output</td><td>Objects</td><td>JSON</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Best for</td><td>PowerShell developers</td><td>Linux/macOS and Bash users</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0359","card":"q-az-900-056-command-line-tools","sec":"az-900-s049","q":"Which platforms do Azure PowerShell and Azure CLI run on?","a":"<p>Both are multi-platform (Windows, Linux, macOS) and scriptable.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0360","card":"q-az-900-056-command-line-tools","sec":"az-900-s049","q":"How do you list resources in Azure PowerShell as a table, as name and location only, as JSON and as HTML?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">PowerShell</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Get-AzResource | Format-Table\nGet-AzResource | Format-Table -Property Name, Location\nGet-AzResource | ConvertTo-Json\nGet-AzResource | ConvertTo-Html</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0361","card":"q-az-900-056-command-line-tools","sec":"az-900-s049","q":"How do you create a VM in Azure PowerShell?","a":"<p>Use <code>New-AzVm</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">PowerShell</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>New-AzVm `\n  -ResourceGroupName &quot;AZ900&quot; `\n  -Name &quot;VM1&quot; `\n  -Location &quot;centralus&quot; `\n  -Image &quot;Ubuntu2204&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0362","card":"q-az-900-056-command-line-tools","sec":"az-900-s049","q":"How do you get a specific resource group in PowerShell and in the Azure CLI?","a":"<p><code>Get-AzResourceGroup</code> in PowerShell, <code>az group show</code> in the CLI.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">PowerShell</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Get-AzResourceGroup -Name &quot;AZ900&quot;</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az group show --name AZ900 --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0363","card":"q-az-900-056-command-line-tools","sec":"az-900-s049","q":"How do you list resources in the Azure CLI as a table with only resource group and name?","a":"<p>Use <code>--output table</code> with a <code>--query</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az resource list --output table --query &quot;[].{ResourceGroup:resourceGroup, Name:name}&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0364","card":"q-az-900-056-command-line-tools","sec":"az-900-s049","q":"How do you create a VM with the Azure CLI?","a":"<p>Use <code>az vm create</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az vm create \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --name VM1 \\\n  --image Ubuntu2204 \\\n  --admin-username azureuser \\\n  --generate-ssh-keys</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0365","card":"q-az-900-057-azure-cloud-shell","sec":"az-900-s050","q":"What is Azure Cloud Shell?","a":"<p>Browser-based PowerShell and Bash with no install. It is already authenticated.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0366","card":"q-az-900-057-azure-cloud-shell","sec":"az-900-s050","q":"Where can you reach Azure Cloud Shell from?","a":"<p>The portal, Azure docs (\"Try It\") and the Azure Mobile App, on any browser, Android, iOS or tablet.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0367","card":"q-az-900-057-azure-cloud-shell","sec":"az-900-s050","q":"What features does Azure Cloud Shell have, and how does it persist sessions?","a":"<p>It switches between PowerShell and Bash, includes a built-in editor and supports file upload/download. It uses a storage account to persist sessions, so installed modules and extensions follow you across devices.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0368","card":"q-az-900-057-azure-cloud-shell","sec":"az-900-s050","q":"How do you check your signed-in account in Cloud Shell, and install and list CLI extensions?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az account show --output table\naz extension add --name azure-devops\naz extension list --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0369","card":"q-az-900-057-azure-cloud-shell","sec":"az-900-s050","q":"How do you open the built-in editor in Azure Cloud Shell?","a":"<p>Run <code>code</code> with a file name.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>code myScript.sh</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0370","card":"q-az-900-058-azure-arc","sec":"az-900-s051","q":"What is Azure Arc?","a":"<p>It extends Azure management and governance to resources outside Azure (on-prem or other clouds).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0371","card":"q-az-900-058-azure-arc","sec":"az-900-s051","q":"How does a machine become an Azure Arc hybrid machine?","a":"<p>Install the Azure Connected Machine Agent on it (single or at scale). It then has an Azure resource ID and can join resource groups.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0372","card":"q-az-900-058-azure-arc","sec":"az-900-s051","q":"What are the Azure Arc features?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Arc feature</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Arc-enabled servers</strong></td><td>Physical/virtual Windows or Linux machines outside Azure</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Arc-enabled Kubernetes</strong></td><td>Kubernetes clusters outside Azure</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Arc-enabled data services</strong></td><td>On top of Arc Kubernetes: SQL Managed Instance, PostgreSQL</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Arc-enabled application services</strong></td><td>On top of Arc Kubernetes: Web Apps, Functions, Logic Apps, API Management, Event Grid</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0373","card":"q-az-900-058-azure-arc","sec":"az-900-s051","q":"How do you install the Azure Connected Machine Agent on a Linux server?","a":"<p>Download the install script and run it.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>wget https://aka.ms/azcmagent -O install_linux_azcmagent.sh\nbash install_linux_azcmagent.sh</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0374","card":"q-az-900-058-azure-arc","sec":"az-900-s051","q":"Which command connects a server to Azure Arc and which verifies the connection?","a":"<p><code>azcmagent connect</code> and <code>azcmagent show</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>azcmagent connect \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --tenant-id &quot;&lt;tenant-id&gt;&quot; \\\n  --location centralus \\\n  --subscription-id &quot;&lt;sub-id&gt;&quot;\nazcmagent show</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0375","card":"q-az-900-058-azure-arc","sec":"az-900-s051","q":"Which Azure CLI commands list Arc-enabled servers and connect and list Arc-enabled Kubernetes clusters?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az connectedmachine list --resource-group AZ900 --output table\naz connectedk8s connect \\\n  --name myK8sCluster \\\n  --resource-group AZ900\naz connectedk8s list --resource-group AZ900 --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0376","card":"q-az-900-059-azure-resource-manager-arm-and-arm-templ","sec":"az-900-s052","q":"What is Azure Resource Manager (ARM)?","a":"<p>The layer that creates and manages all Azure resources. It is declarative (you say what, not how). Every tool (Portal, PowerShell, CLI, Visual Studio) goes through it, so results are consistent.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0377","card":"q-az-900-059-azure-resource-manager-arm-and-arm-templ","sec":"az-900-s052","q":"What are ARM templates?","a":"<p>JSON files declaring what ARM should do, for repeatable and predictable deployments.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0378","card":"q-az-900-059-azure-resource-manager-arm-and-arm-templ","sec":"az-900-s052","q":"What are the sections of an ARM template?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>$schema</code>: template language version.</li>\n  <li><code>contentVersion</code>.</li>\n  <li><code>parameters</code>: values at deploy time.</li>\n  <li><code>variables</code>: reusable values.</li>\n  <li><code>resources</code>.</li>\n  <li><code>outputs</code>: values returned.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0379","card":"q-az-900-059-azure-resource-manager-arm-and-arm-templ","sec":"az-900-s052","q":"How do you declare a VM name parameter with a default value in an ARM template?","a":"<p>Add it under <code>parameters</code> with a type and <code>defaultValue</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JSON</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&quot;parameters&quot;: {\n  &quot;vmName&quot;: {\n    &quot;type&quot;: &quot;string&quot;,\n    &quot;defaultValue&quot;: &quot;VM1&quot;\n  },</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0380","card":"q-az-900-059-azure-resource-manager-arm-and-arm-templ","sec":"az-900-s052","q":"How do you put tags on a VM resource in an ARM template?","a":"<p>Add a <code>tags</code> object to the resource.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JSON</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&quot;tags&quot;: {\n  &quot;department&quot;: &quot;marketing&quot;,\n  &quot;usage&quot;: &quot;AZ900 live training&quot;\n},</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0381","card":"q-az-900-059-azure-resource-manager-arm-and-arm-templ","sec":"az-900-s052","q":"In an ARM template, how do you make the <code>location</code> parameter default to the resource group's location?","a":"<p>Set its <code>defaultValue</code> to <code>[resourceGroup().location]</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JSON</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&quot;location&quot;: {\n  &quot;type&quot;: &quot;string&quot;,\n  &quot;defaultValue&quot;: &quot;[resourceGroup().location]&quot;\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0382","card":"q-az-900-059-azure-resource-manager-arm-and-arm-templ","sec":"az-900-s052","q":"In an ARM template VM resource, how do you set the VM size and the Ubuntu image?","a":"<p>Set <code>vmSize</code> under <code>hardwareProfile</code>, and the Canonical image under <code>imageReference</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JSON</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&quot;hardwareProfile&quot;: { &quot;vmSize&quot;: &quot;Standard_D2s_v3&quot; },\n&quot;imageReference&quot;: {\n  &quot;publisher&quot;: &quot;Canonical&quot;,\n  &quot;offer&quot;: &quot;0001-com-ubuntu-server-jammy&quot;,\n  &quot;sku&quot;: &quot;22_04-lts&quot;,\n  &quot;version&quot;: &quot;latest&quot;\n},</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0383","card":"q-az-900-059-azure-resource-manager-arm-and-arm-templ","sec":"az-900-s052","q":"In an ARM template VM resource, how do you set the computer name and admin user?","a":"<p>Use <code>osProfile</code> with <code>computerName</code> and <code>adminUsername</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JSON</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&quot;osProfile&quot;: {\n  &quot;computerName&quot;: &quot;[parameters(&#x27;vmName&#x27;)]&quot;,\n  &quot;adminUsername&quot;: &quot;azureuser&quot;\n},</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0384","card":"q-az-900-060-azure-resource-manager-arm-and-arm-templ","sec":"az-900-s052","q":"How do you deploy an ARM template and pass a parameter with the Azure CLI?","a":"<p>Use <code>az deployment group create</code> with <code>--template-file</code> and <code>--parameters</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az deployment group create \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --template-file azuredeploy.json \\\n  --parameters vmName=VM1</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0385","card":"q-az-900-060-azure-resource-manager-arm-and-arm-templ","sec":"az-900-s052","q":"How do you override several ARM template parameters at deploy time?","a":"<p>Pass several <code>name=value</code> pairs after <code>--parameters</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>--parameters vmName=VM2 location=eastus</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0386","card":"q-az-900-060-azure-resource-manager-arm-and-arm-templ","sec":"az-900-s052","q":"How do you export a resource group as an ARM template with the Azure CLI?","a":"<p>Use <code>az group export</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az group export --name AZ900 --output json &gt; exported-template.json</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0387","card":"q-az-900-060-azure-resource-manager-arm-and-arm-templ","sec":"az-900-s052","q":"How do you validate an ARM template before deploying and list deployments?","a":"<p>Use <code>az deployment group validate</code> and <code>az deployment group list</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az deployment group validate \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --template-file azuredeploy.json\naz deployment group list --resource-group AZ900 --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0388","card":"q-az-900-060-azure-resource-manager-arm-and-arm-templ","sec":"az-900-s052","q":"Which Azure management tool fits each need: visual management, PowerShell automation, Bash, access from anywhere, repeatable deployments, hybrid management?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Type</th><th>Best for</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Portal</td><td>Web GUI</td><td>Visual management, dashboards</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>PowerShell</td><td>CLI cmdlets</td><td>PowerShell developers, automation</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>CLI</td><td>CLI commands</td><td>Linux/macOS, Bash</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Cloud Shell</td><td>Browser CLI</td><td>Access from anywhere</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>ARM templates</td><td>JSON IaC</td><td>Repeatable deployments</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Arc</td><td>Hybrid management</td><td>Extend Azure to on-prem and other clouds</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0389","card":"q-az-900-061-12-monitoring-tools","sec":"az-900-s053","q":"What are the three Azure monitoring tools and their purpose?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Nature</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Azure Advisor</strong></td><td>Best-practice recommendations before problems occur</td><td>Proactive</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Azure Service Health</strong></td><td>Azure platform incidents and planned maintenance</td><td>Tracks Azure-side issues</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Azure Monitor</strong></td><td>Real-time metrics, Application Insights, Log Analytics</td><td>Real-time and historical</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0390","card":"q-az-900-062-azure-advisor","sec":"az-900-s054","q":"What does Azure Advisor do?","a":"<p>It helps keep resources highly available and efficient, and can sometimes fix problems automatically.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0391","card":"q-az-900-062-azure-advisor","sec":"az-900-s054","q":"What is the Azure Advisor score?","a":"<p>A 0 to 100% score of how well you follow best practices, by category, with a monthly history.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0392","card":"q-az-900-062-azure-advisor","sec":"az-900-s054","q":"What are the Azure Advisor categories?","a":"<p>Security, Reliability, Operational Excellence, Performance and Cost.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0393","card":"q-az-900-062-azure-advisor","sec":"az-900-s054","q":"What are the two remediation types in Azure Advisor?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Automated</strong>: the Fix It button, for example installing a missing agent.</li>\n  <li><strong>Manual</strong>: step-by-step instructions.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0394","card":"q-az-900-062-azure-advisor","sec":"az-900-s054","q":"How do you list Azure Advisor recommendations, filtered by category, with the CLI?","a":"<p>Use <code>az advisor recommendation list</code>, with <code>--category</code> for a filter.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az advisor recommendation list --output table\naz advisor recommendation list \\\n  --category Security \\\n  --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0395","card":"q-az-900-062-azure-advisor","sec":"az-900-s054","q":"How do you list only high-impact Azure Advisor recommendations?","a":"<p>Use a <code>--query</code> that filters on <code>impact=='High'</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az advisor recommendation list \\\n  --query &quot;[?impact==&#x27;High&#x27;].{Category:category, Impact:impact, Problem:shortDescription.problem}&quot; \\\n  --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0396","card":"q-az-900-062-azure-advisor","sec":"az-900-s054","q":"How do you find cost savings and dismiss a recommendation in Azure Advisor with the CLI?","a":"<p>Use <code>--category Cost</code> to list savings, and <code>az advisor recommendation disable</code> to dismiss one.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az advisor recommendation list \\\n  --category Cost \\\n  --query &quot;[].{Resource:resourceMetadata.resourceId, Savings:extendedProperties.savingsAmount}&quot; \\\n  --output table\naz advisor recommendation disable \\\n  --ids &quot;&lt;recommendation-resource-id&gt;&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0397","card":"q-az-900-062-azure-advisor","sec":"az-900-s054","q":"In Azure Advisor, which command shows the Advisor configuration?","a":"<p><code>az advisor configuration list</code> shows it.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az advisor configuration list --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0398","card":"q-az-900-063-azure-service-health","sec":"az-900-s055","q":"What does Azure Service Health report?","a":"<p>Problems with Azure itself, scoped to the regions where you have resources.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0399","card":"q-az-900-063-azure-service-health","sec":"az-900-s055","q":"What are the three parts of Azure Service Health?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Service incidents</strong>: unexpected issues.</li>\n  <li><strong>Planned maintenance</strong>: upcoming work that may affect you.</li>\n  <li><strong>Health history</strong>: past incidents with summary, times and root cause analysis. Download as PDF, share a link, or track on mobile.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0400","card":"q-az-900-063-azure-service-health","sec":"az-900-s055","q":"How do you list current Azure service health events with <code>az rest</code>?","a":"<p>Send a GET to the <code>Microsoft.ResourceHealth/events</code> endpoint of the subscription.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az rest --method GET \\\n  --uri &quot;https://management.azure.com/subscriptions/&lt;sub-id&gt;/providers/Microsoft.ResourceHealth/events?api-version=2022-10-01&quot; \\\n  --query &quot;value[].{Name:name, Status:properties.status, Impact:properties.impactType, Region:properties.impactedServiceRegion}&quot; \\\n  --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0401","card":"q-az-900-063-azure-service-health","sec":"az-900-s055","q":"How do you check the resource health of a specific VM from the CLI?","a":"<p>Use <code>az resource show</code> with the <code>availabilityStatuses/current</code> resource ID.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az resource show \\\n  --ids &quot;/subscriptions/&lt;sub-id&gt;/resourceGroups/AZ900/providers/Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/VM1/providers/Microsoft.ResourceHealth/availabilityStatuses/current&quot; \\\n  --api-version 2022-10-01 \\\n  --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0402","card":"q-az-900-063-azure-service-health","sec":"az-900-s055","q":"In Azure Service Health, how do you list only health advisories with the CLI?","a":"<p>Call the Resource Health events API with <code>az rest</code> and filter on the event type <code>HealthAdvisory</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az rest --method GET \\\n  --uri &quot;https://management.azure.com/subscriptions/&lt;sub-id&gt;/providers/Microsoft.ResourceHealth/events?api-version=2022-10-01&amp;\\$filter=properties/eventType eq &#x27;HealthAdvisory&#x27;&quot; \\\n  --output json</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0403","card":"q-az-900-064-azure-monitor","sec":"az-900-s056","q":"What are the three parts of Azure Monitor?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Metrics</strong>: real-time performance data (CPU, disk, network).</li>\n  <li><strong>Application Insights</strong>: automatic instrumentation for web apps, Functions and VMs.</li>\n  <li><strong>Log Analytics</strong>: historical analysis with Kusto Query Language (KQL).</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0404","card":"q-az-900-064-azure-monitor","sec":"az-900-s056","q":"How do you build a chart in Azure Monitor Metrics?","a":"<p>Choose a scope, combine metrics that share a unit, pick a chart type (line, area, bar) and pin it to a dashboard.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0405","card":"q-az-900-064-azure-monitor","sec":"az-900-s056","q":"What does Application Insights track, and when is it available?","a":"<p>It tracks failed requests, response times, availability and page views. It is available as soon as you create a web app, and supports on-prem VMs through the Application Insights Agent.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0406","card":"q-az-900-064-azure-monitor","sec":"az-900-s056","q":"Which query language does Log Analytics use?","a":"<p>Kusto Query Language (KQL).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0407","card":"q-az-900-064-azure-monitor","sec":"az-900-s056","q":"How do you view a VM's CPU percentage for the last hour with the Azure CLI?","a":"<p>Use <code>az monitor metrics list</code> with <code>--metric</code> and <code>--interval PT1H</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az monitor metrics list \\\n  --resource &quot;/subscriptions/&lt;sub-id&gt;/resourceGroups/AZ900/providers/Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/VM1&quot; \\\n  --metric &quot;Percentage CPU&quot; \\\n  --interval PT1H \\\n  --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0408","card":"q-az-900-064-azure-monitor","sec":"az-900-s056","q":"How do you create an Azure Monitor metric alert for CPU above 80%?","a":"<p>Use <code>az monitor metrics alert create</code> with a <code>--condition</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az monitor metrics alert create \\\n  --name &quot;HighCPUAlert&quot; \\\n  --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --scopes &quot;/subscriptions/&lt;sub-id&gt;/resourceGroups/AZ900/providers/Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/VM1&quot; \\\n  --condition &quot;avg Percentage CPU &gt; 80&quot; \\\n  --description &quot;Alert when CPU exceeds 80%&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0409","card":"q-az-900-064-azure-monitor","sec":"az-900-s056","q":"How do you enable Application Insights on a web app with the Azure CLI?","a":"<p>Create a component with <code>az monitor app-insights component create</code>, then set the instrumentation key as an app setting.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az monitor app-insights component create \\\n  --app az900appinsights \\\n  --location centralus \\\n  --resource-group AZ900\naz webapp config appsettings set \\\n  --name az900wa --resource-group AZ900 \\\n  --settings APPINSIGHTS_INSTRUMENTATIONKEY=&quot;&lt;instrumentation-key&gt;&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0410","card":"q-az-900-064-azure-monitor","sec":"az-900-s056","q":"Which KQL query shows average CPU usage over the last 24 hours as a time chart?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">KQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Perf\n| where ObjectName == &quot;Processor&quot; and CounterName == &quot;% Processor Time&quot;\n| where TimeGenerated &gt; ago(24h)\n| summarize AvgCPU = avg(CounterValue) by bin(TimeGenerated, 1h)\n| render timechart</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0411","card":"q-az-900-064-azure-monitor","sec":"az-900-s056","q":"Which KQL query counts failed Application Insights requests per hour and name?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">KQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>requests\n| where success == false\n| where timestamp &gt; ago(24h)\n| summarize FailedCount = count() by bin(timestamp, 1h), name\n| order by FailedCount desc</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0412","card":"q-az-900-064-azure-monitor","sec":"az-900-s056","q":"Which KQL query shows average disk reads and writes per second over 48 hours?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">KQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Perf\n| where ObjectName == &quot;LogicalDisk&quot;\n| where CounterName in (&quot;Disk Reads/sec&quot;, &quot;Disk Writes/sec&quot;)\n| where TimeGenerated &gt; ago(48h)\n| summarize avg(CounterValue) by CounterName, bin(TimeGenerated, 1h)\n| render timechart</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0413","card":"q-az-900-064-azure-monitor","sec":"az-900-s056","q":"In Azure Monitor, how do you view a VM's disk read and write bytes with the CLI?","a":"<p>Use <code>az monitor metrics list</code> with the metrics <code>Disk Read Bytes</code> and <code>Disk Write Bytes</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az monitor metrics list \\\n  --resource &quot;/subscriptions/&lt;sub-id&gt;/resourceGroups/AZ900/providers/Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/VM1&quot; \\\n  --metric &quot;Disk Read Bytes&quot; &quot;Disk Write Bytes&quot; \\\n  --interval PT1H \\\n  --output table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0414","card":"q-az-900-065-dan-storage-identity-availability","sec":"az-900-s057","q":"In the Azure scenario with four VMs and hundreds of GB of images used from mobile devices, how is each requirement solved?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Requirement</th><th>Solution</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Frequently used images</td><td>Blob Storage, <strong>Hot</strong> tier</td><td>Low access cost</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Archived images for regulatory compliance</td><td>Blob Storage, <strong>Archive</strong> tier</td><td>Lowest storage cost, rarely read</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Migrate hundreds of GB of images</td><td><strong>Data Box Disk</strong></td><td>Microsoft ships SSDs, you copy and ship back</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Secure mobile access, protect against a lost device</td><td><strong>Passwordless with Microsoft Authenticator</strong> and biometrics</td><td>No stored password</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Survive data center failures</td><td><strong>Availability sets</strong></td><td>Fault domains for racks, update domains for reboots</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Survive natural disasters</td><td>Deploy to <strong>both regions of a region pair</strong></td><td>Regions are geographically separated, and Microsoft avoids impacting both at once</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0415","card":"q-az-900-065-dan-storage-identity-availability","sec":"az-900-s057","q":"Which Azure feature protects a VM app from a data center failure, and what do fault domains and update domains cover?","a":"<p>Availability sets. Fault domains cover racks, update domains cover reboots.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0416","card":"q-az-900-065-dan-storage-identity-availability","sec":"az-900-s057","q":"Which Azure CLI command creates an availability set and then a VM in it?","a":"<p><code>az vm availability-set create</code>, then <code>az vm create</code> with <code>--availability-set</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az vm availability-set create \\\n  --resource-group DanApp --name DanAvailSet \\\n  --platform-fault-domain-count 2 --platform-update-domain-count 3\naz vm create --resource-group DanApp --name DanVM1 \\\n  --image Ubuntu2204 --availability-set DanAvailSet \\\n  --admin-username azureuser --generate-ssh-keys</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0417","card":"q-az-900-065-dan-storage-identity-availability","sec":"az-900-s057","q":"How do you create a GRS storage account and a container for active images with the Azure CLI?","a":"<p>Use <code>az storage account create</code> with <code>--sku Standard_GRS</code>, then <code>az storage container create</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az storage account create --name danstorage --resource-group DanApp --location centralus --sku Standard_GRS\naz storage container create --name active-images --account-name danstorage</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0418","card":"q-az-900-065-dan-storage-identity-availability","sec":"az-900-s057","q":"How do you upload a blob straight to the Archive tier?","a":"<p>Use <code>az storage blob upload</code> with <code>--tier Archive</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az storage blob upload --account-name danstorage --container-name archived-images \\\n  --name old-record.jpg --file ./old-record.jpg --tier Archive</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0419","card":"q-az-900-065-dan-storage-identity-availability","sec":"az-900-s057","q":"How do you enable the Microsoft Authenticator passwordless method for a tenant with <code>az rest</code>?","a":"<p>PATCH the <code>microsoftAuthenticator</code> authentication method configuration with state enabled.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az rest --method PATCH \\\n  --uri &quot;https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/policies/authenticationMethodsPolicy/authenticationMethodConfigurations/microsoftAuthenticator&quot; \\\n  --headers &quot;Content-Type=application/json&quot; \\\n  --body &#x27;{&quot;state&quot;: &quot;enabled&quot;}&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0420","card":"q-az-900-066-will-pricing-performance-protection","sec":"az-900-s058","q":"In the Azure scenario of a web app deployed to multiple regions, how is each requirement solved?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Requirement</th><th>Solution</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Cost estimate</td><td><strong>Pricing Calculator</strong></td><td>New web apps, not a migration, so not TCO. Exportable and shareable</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Prevent accidental deletion</td><td><strong>Do Not Delete lock</strong></td><td>Applies to everyone regardless of RBAC role, even if roles change later</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Identical deployments</td><td><strong>ARM templates</strong></td><td>Declarative JSON, easy to add regions</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Monitoring and alerts</td><td><strong>Azure Monitor + Application Insights</strong></td><td>Automatic web app metrics, alerts for anomalies, shareable dashboards</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0421","card":"q-az-900-066-will-pricing-performance-protection","sec":"az-900-s058","q":"Why use the Pricing Calculator and not the TCO Calculator to estimate the cost of new web apps?","a":"<p>These are new web apps, not a migration, so TCO does not apply. The Pricing Calculator output is exportable and shareable.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0422","card":"q-az-900-066-will-pricing-performance-protection","sec":"az-900-s058","q":"Why does a Do Not Delete lock stop interns who have RBAC access from deleting a web app?","a":"<p>It applies to everyone regardless of RBAC role, even if roles change later.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0423","card":"q-az-900-066-will-pricing-performance-protection","sec":"az-900-s058","q":"Why are ARM templates the right way to deploy a web app identically in many regions?","a":"<p>They are declarative JSON, so results are identical and it is easy to add regions.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0424","card":"q-az-900-067-will-pricing-performance-protection","sec":"az-900-s058","q":"How do you deploy the same ARM template to a second region with different parameters?","a":"<p>Run <code>az deployment group create</code> per region with different <code>--parameters</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az deployment group create --resource-group WillApp-EastUS \\\n  --template-file webapp-template.json \\\n  --parameters appName=willapp-eastus location=eastus\naz deployment group create --resource-group WillApp-WestEU \\\n  --template-file webapp-template.json \\\n  --parameters appName=willapp-westeu location=westeurope</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0425","card":"q-az-900-067-will-pricing-performance-protection","sec":"az-900-s058","q":"How do you protect a web app with a Do Not Delete lock with the Azure CLI?","a":"<p>Use <code>az lock create</code> with <code>--lock-type CanNotDelete</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az lock create --name &quot;DoNotDelete&quot; --lock-type CanNotDelete \\\n  --resource-group WillApp-EastUS --resource-name willapp-eastus \\\n  --resource-type Microsoft.Web/sites</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0426","card":"q-az-900-067-will-pricing-performance-protection","sec":"az-900-s058","q":"How do you create an Application Insights component and an alert on web app response time above 5 seconds?","a":"<p>Use <code>az monitor app-insights component create</code> and <code>az monitor metrics alert create</code> with <code>avg HttpResponseTime &gt; 5</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>az monitor app-insights component create \\\n  --app willapp-insights --location eastus --resource-group WillApp-EastUS\naz monitor metrics alert create \\\n  --name &quot;HighResponseTime&quot; --resource-group WillApp-EastUS \\\n  --scopes &quot;/subscriptions/&lt;sub-id&gt;/resourceGroups/WillApp-EastUS/providers/Microsoft.Web/sites/willapp-eastus&quot; \\\n  --condition &quot;avg HttpResponseTime &gt; 5&quot; \\\n  --description &quot;Alert when response time exceeds 5 seconds&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"az-900-f0427","card":"q-az-900-067-will-pricing-performance-protection","sec":"az-900-s058","q":"In the multi-region ARM template for a web app, how is the web app tied to its App Service plan?","a":"<p>It uses <code>dependsOn</code> on the plan and <code>serverFarmId</code> set with <code>resourceId</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JSON</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&quot;dependsOn&quot;: [&quot;[concat(parameters(&#x27;appName&#x27;), &#x27;-plan&#x27;)]&quot;],\n&quot;properties&quot;: {\n  &quot;serverFarmId&quot;: &quot;[resourceId(&#x27;Microsoft.Web/serverfarms&#x27;, concat(parameters(&#x27;appName&#x27;), &#x27;-plan&#x27;))]&quot;\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true}];
